iclr-2026-0853a1e684f7,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 12,32,以三组 speech-captioned montage 对比 OmniHuman-1 与 Ours 的语义相关动作。,double_column,90.00|84.34|522.00|391.22,qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,2,1,"Figure 12: Qualitative comparison with OmniHuman-1 (Lin et al., 2025b), a state-of-the-art model representing the predominant conditioning scheme of audio cross-attention and image reference attention. For each pair of examples, our model (bottom row) generates actions with higher semantic consistency to the speech prompt than the baseline (top row). For example, our model correctly depicts a character applying makeup and a glowing crystal ball as described in the speech, actions which are absent in the baseline’s results.",78,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,,,,,color,8,#74604F|#464A39|#6A4A32|#3F3120|#A18F81|#797161|#B4A696|#8B7772,0.5163,,,
iclr-2026-0853a1e684f7,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 13,33,展示 rapid motion 手部 artifact、large head turn 的身份退化和 over-articulated gestures。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|257.64,other,1,1,1,"Figure 13: Limitations of our method. Despite its strong performance, our method exhibits limita- tions in both synthesis and reasoning. On the synthesis level, the model can struggle with fine details during rapid movements, leading to hand artifacts (row 1) and degraded facial identity during large head turns (row 2). Separately, on the reasoning level, the agent can generate motions that, while plausible, are occasionally over-articulated (e.g., excessive gesturing), lacking the subtlety required for cinematic performance.",77,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,1,0,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,9.963,9.963,color,8,#4A1109|#738456|#94A479|#73614C|#7E3927|#414736|#9F6548|#ACAA87,0.6558,,,
iclr-2026-09d94b8d6d44,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 1,4,三阶段 position-ID architecture 与 PCA、RSA、CMA supporting evidence 的总览,double_column,90.00|34.46|522.00|341.34,pipeline|architecture,4,2,1,"Figure 1: Overview of position ID architecture and supporting evidence. We identify three process- ing stages: ID retrieval heads that retrieve the position ID of objects described in the prompt, ID selection heads that select the position ID for a target object, and feature retrieval heads that use this position ID to retrieve the features of the target object. These stages are revealed both by (b,c) representational and (d) causal mediation analyses (see text for explanation).",77,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|DejaVuSans|ArialMT|CourierNew-Bold|OpenSans-Bold|DejaVuSans-Oblique,1.529,4.95,8.966,color,8,#6896A3|#ED9C26|#AFD7BE|#EAEDF7|#483786|#EB99AD|#E74579|#41E1B2,0.1837,,,
iclr-2026-09d94b8d6d44,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 2,7,3x3/2x2 grid 下 relative、absolute position 与 feature 的 RSA 对比,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|235.25,scatter|qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 2: Testing for relative vs. absolute spatial coding. Left: Example of each grid condition with centrally located object circled. Right: RSA results showing second-order correlation of last token embeddings (Qwen2-VL) with relative position, absolute position, and object features.",39,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,0,1,1,0,0,2,DejaVuSans|DejaVuSans-Bold|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,1.529,4.583,9.963,color,8,#EAEFEC|#6BBC4D|#A4EDC7|#833D96|#EE1F23|#5F68A2|#DFC0CE|#E15DA0,0.2418,,,
