iclr-2026-09d94b8d6d44,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 5,9,把 scene-description position IDs 注入 spatial reasoning 的 before/after accuracy,single_column,311.00|20.00|588.00|260.75,other,1,1,1,Figure 5: Intervention performance on spatial reasoning task.,8,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,DejaVuSans,2.308,5.918,7.587,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-09d94b8d6d44,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 6,9,high/low feature entropy stimuli 与 prompt/last-token position RSA,double_column,90.00|286.31|522.00|593.19,qualitative_grid,4,4,1,"Figure 6: Binding error analysis showing effect of feature entropy on position ID mechanisms. We next investigated the role that position IDs and visual symbolic mechanisms play in binding errors. Specifically, we analyzed how position IDs influence the model’s ability to bind features to objects or locations, using a scene description task with varying feature entropy – a factor known to impact binding errors (Greff et al., 2020; Campbell et al., 2024). Details of the generation process are provided in Appendix A.5.4 and examples of low (resp. high ) entropy stimuli are shown in Figure 6b (resp. 6a). Our results (Figure 6) show that entropy level strongly affects position ID representations at two critical stages: ID retrieval Figure 6c) and ID selection (Figure 6d). We observe that lower entropy leads to less accurate ID retrieval and more ambiguous ID selection,",141,7,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,0,1,1,1,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|DejaVuSans|DejaVuSans-Bold|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|DejaVuSans-Oblique,1.605,9.963,9.963,color,8,#769DE1|#FA9794|#F97279|#F2EEF4|#FBCBCD|#C8E2F7|#6C23B1|#FA3134,0.1133,,,
iclr-2026-09d94b8d6d44,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 7,10,entropy 条件下 position-ID mechanism failure 与 binding-error accuracy 的总体联系,single_column,311.00|20.00|588.00|210.25,other,1,1,1,Figure 7: Link between binding errors and failure of position ID mechanisms.,12,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,,,,,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-09d94b8d6d44,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 8,14,relative/absolute position coding 的四种 grid stimulus condition,double_column,90.00|268.61|522.00|575.49,other,1,1,1,"Figure 8: Stimulus condition for characterizing relative vs absolute position IDs. To determine whether position IDs use relative or absolute position coding, we designed an exper- iment using a 3×3 object grid. We created four different 2×2 sub-arrangements of objects, each positioned within different quadrants of the larger grid (Figure 8). Crucially, across all four arrange- ments, one object was always placed at the same absolute position (the center position).",72,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,7.97,9.963,9.963,color,8,#69BD45|#EE1F23|#773E98|#3D53A2|#E9E0DA|#A582B0|#EE3235|#8EC971,0.1549,,,
iclr-2026-09d94b8d6d44,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 9,15,binding-error 数据集的 2x2/3x3 high-entropy 与 low-entropy 配置,double_column,90.00|52.51|522.00|359.39,image_montage,1,3,1,"Figure 9: Image configurations for investigating binding errors. To investigate the role of position IDs in binding errors, we created datasets varying in grid size and entropy. Low entropy datasets used all possible conjunctions from limited color and shape sets, while high entropy datasets used the most distinct conjunctions from larger sets. The 2×2 grid (280×280 pixels; 4 objects) used 2 colors × 2 shapes for low entropy and the 4 most distinct conjunctions from 4 colors × 4 shapes for high entropy (both involving 100 trials/combination; 1600 total). The 3×3 grid (392×392 pixels; 9 objects) used 9 conjunctions from 3 colors × 3 shapes for low entropy and 9 objects with unique color and shape for high entropy (both involving 50 trials/combination; 4,050 per condition).",130,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,0,1,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,2.77,9.963,9.963,color,8,#0000FF|#00FF00|#E6DECD|#FF0000|#7B23C0|#B0FFB0|#0F0FFF|#DC92A9,0.2539,,,
