iclr-2026-106be5e431a2,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,以绿色 discovered edges 与红色 potential edges 对比 pairwise reweighting、realignment 和 correspondence generation。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|245.12,conceptual_diagram|qualitative_grid,3,4,1,"Figure 1: (Top) Examples of multi-view data, including noisy pairs I –T . (Bottom) Illustration of 4 4 three paradigms for handling noisy correspondence, where green edges denote discovered corre- spondences and red edges indicate potential but undiscovered ones. (a) Pairwise reweighting, which applies robust contrastive losses to down-weight potentially noisy pairs during training but retains the original correspondences unchanged; (b) Pairwise realignment, which reassigns each sample to a more plausible cross-view counterpart; (c) Correspondence generation (Ours), which directly uncovers latent correspondences and filters out noise.",85,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR7,9.963,0,0,1,1,0,0,2,TimesNewRomanPSMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,3.526,6.099,9.963,color,5,#D0E4D5|#DCEAF7|#625C41|#8FAD78|#C3CBBB,0.8564,,,
