iclr-2026-24987e898413,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,对比 natural-language names、peptide blocks 与 small-molecule blocks；以 imatinib 展示功能和 synthesis token。,double_column,90.00|20.00|523.65|238.31,other,1,2,1,"Figure 1: mCLM adopts a modular chemical vocabulary, which uses synthesis robot-friendly molecu- lar building blocks as tokens together with natural language tokens. Compared with using natural language names, SMILES strings, or holistic embeddings for whole molecules, this building block level of tokenization better enables the prediction of compounds with improved properties, and guarantees automated synthesizability a priori, thus building a direct link between the digital and physical worlds. This approach stands to substantially enable AI-guided discovery of new small molecules with targeted functions.",84,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,Nunito-ExtraLight|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,1.665,5.506,9.963,color,8,#90919C|#6E6E81|#BFD5C1|#CEE6D7|#D0BABF|#9AB5AA|#F3E8DC|#CEF2E0,0.5437,,,
iclr-2026-24987e898413,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 2,4,总览 text–molecule bilingual mCLM：GNN、Transformer decoder、chemical similarity search、function/synthesis knowledge。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|312.93,pipeline|architecture,1,1,1,"Figure 2: An overview of the mCLM. It is a multimodal chemical-language model that tokenizes molecules into synthesis robot-friendly building blocks, thus creating a direct link between the digital and physical worlds. After being trained on datasets consisting of properties, functions and synthesis data, the mCLM can conduct critical chemical reasoning through an iterative refinement process.",56,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,MyriadPro-Semibold|MyriadPro-Regular|Nunito-ExtraLight|MyriadPro-It|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|MyriadPro-BoldIt,1.038,6.783,11.004,color,6,#3D4A5A|#F99C8A|#FFDDA6|#BD8688|#596271|#C6BFB0,0.7154,,,
iclr-2026-24987e898413,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 3,5,synthesis-guaranteed tokenizer → coverage check → rule-based fallback；列出三类 coupling。,double_column,89.64|173.90|522.34|480.78,pipeline,1,1,1,"Figure 3: An overview of the tokenization process. A functional molecule is first processed by the synthesis-guaranteed tokenizer to produce a set of building blocks compatible with automated modular synthesis. These blocks are then evaluated via a structure coverage check to determine whether they fully reconstruct the original molecule. If coverage is complete, the blocks are used directly for pretraining. Otherwise, the molecule is reprocessed using a rule-based tokenizer to ensure full representation for training purposes.",76,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|Nunito-ExtraLight|MyriadPro-Regular|Nunito-ExtraLightItalic,3.35,9.963,9.963,color,8,#3B4959|#868E9A|#485464|#DBB6CB|#606B7E|#E0DBE0|#97A9B1|#8D7B92,0.3907,,,
