iclr-2026-3f0f7132b565,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,table,appendix,appendix,Table 13,18,"Account for speech/text units, total sequence length, and derived FLOPs reduction.",double_column,90.00|212.22|522.00|463.66,table,1,1,1,"Table 13: Token accounting under the compute-controlled setting. Interleaved speech–text data follow a 1:2 word ratio. Due to higher speech token density, the baseline allocates 0.77 speech tokens versus 0.23 text tokens within the interleaved portion. LST compresses speech tokens via 4→1 patching, reducing the overall sequence length from 3.00 to 2.42 (∼20% FLOPs reduction).",62,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|CMMI10|CMSY10,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|CMSY10|CMMI10,7.97,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-4019795d726c,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,概念性对照：EEG/ECG 的 brain/heart 中心协调，与 attention 的全连接图及 CoTAR 的 core-token 图。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|201.64,architecture|conceptual_diagram,4,2,1,"Figure 1: (a): Illustration of Temporal dependencies within each channel, and channel dependencies across channels. (b): Interaction between channels in EEG/ECG signals is centrally controlled by the brain/heart. (c): Attention module is a decentralized structure, where each token attends to all other tokens equally. (d): The proposed Core Token Aggregation-Redistribution (CoTAR) module operates in a centralized manner, with a core token as a proxy.",66,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,9.963,9.963,color,8,#F7C399|#EF9989|#DF545B|#F8D4BA|#88C8CA|#715057|#F6C398|#9D919C,0.5904,,,
iclr-2026-4019795d726c,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,4,同一抽象层级展示 standard attention 的 pairwise 路径和 CoTAR 的 aggregation/redistribution 路径。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|233.91,tree|conceptual_diagram,1,1,1,"Figure 2: Illustration of attention and Core Token Aggregation-Redistribution (CoTAR). Attention is organized in a decentralized way where each token directly interacts with all tokens, introducing a Quadratic complexity. CoTAR first aggregates a core token and then redistributes it across channels to facilitate centralized channel interaction, bringing only Linear complexity.",50,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-MediItal|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,7.97,9.963,11.955,color,8,#E9F1FC|#FFF4D6|#B4A092|#D0E2C9|#FEF3D5|#E9F1FB|#FEF4D5|#E8F1FC,0.812,,,
iclr-2026-4019795d726c,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 3,5,展示 TeCh 的 Temporal/Channel embedding、CoTAR Transformer encoders、branch averaging、fusion 与 logits。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|227.73,pipeline|qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 3: Overview of TeCh. MedTS signals X ∈ RT×C are embedded into Temporal embedding and Channel embedding. Then, each embedding is processed using Transformer encoders, with attention replaced by CoTAR. The final output representation from each branch is averaged across channels and added, then projected to the final predicted logits Yˆ ∈ RK.",53,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMMI7|CMMI10|CMSY10,9.963,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,9.963,9.963,color,8,#F2E6D8|#F1B3A2|#749999|#F9D5B8|#C6E0DA|#A5B5B1|#BE958A|#F2E5D7,0.3916,,,
