iclr-2026-557a29cfb5fa,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,1,右侧流程图对比 prior compositional diffusion 的 mode averaging 与 CDGS 的 search/prune/select；宽幅浮动图。,double_column,90.00|348.06|522.00|654.94,pipeline|qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,3,1,"short-horizon local distributions to sam- Figure 1: Compositional Diffusion with Guided ple long-horizon global plans [66, 44, Search (CDGS) composes short-horizon plan distri- 40]—e.g., chaining skills for task plan- butions to sample long-horizon goal-directed plans di- ning, connecting images into panoramas, rectly at inference. Unlike na¨ıve compositional sam- or stitching clips into videos. While this pling, it explores diverse plans and filters locally in- improves data-efficiency and allows ex- consistent paths to avoid “mode averaging”, yielding trapolation beyond training data, it intro- globally coherent plans.",88,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|Aptos|Aptos-Bold|NimbusMonL-Regu|CambriaMath,1.242,9.963,11.955,color,8,#DEF1F9|#AEDDF1|#546B7B|#96D3E7|#C1DEEB|#79BAC0|#98F3DD|#E5F4FA,0.3344,,,
iclr-2026-557a29cfb5fa,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 2,2,顶部全宽展示机器人多步 hook/cube、512×4608 panorama、350-frame video 三类应用。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|266.90,image_montage,1,2,1,"Figure 2: Applications of CDGS. (Top) Long horizon motion planning: CDGS discovers a valid multi-step plan to move the blue cube to the green cube’s original position via : (1) using the hook to pull blue cube in workspace, (2) displace the green cube to make space and (3) moving the blue cube to the target position. (Mid) CDGS generates coherent panoramic images. (Bottom) CDGS can stitch short clips to generate consistent, longer videos.",74,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,Aptos-Italic|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|Aptos|Aptos-Bold|Calibri-Italic,7.844,7.844,9.963,color,8,#7E6055|#403329|#1C9018|#938F8A|#B4B7A3|#1F5C32|#952F2B|#2EAE18,0.4976,,,
iclr-2026-557a29cfb5fa,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,theory,main,Figure 3,3,四个并列 1D domain 小图从 naive composition 到 resampling+pruning，展示两条可行路径与 infeasible overlaps。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|165.01,qualitative_grid,4,4,1,"Figure 3: Running example. (a) Consider a 1D-domain of x 1:7 variable distributions and y 1:6 { } { } feasible directed transitions between the variables. There are two feasible long-horizon plans from start (x ) to goal (x ): one through the top and one through the bottom. (b) in naive-composition, 1 7 sampled plans may choose to start in the top and end at the bottom, or vice versa. When this happens, the intermediate models y will average the modes of intermediate variables x to 2:5 2:6 { } { } satisfy both constraints, manifesting in infeasible transitions (red) (c) adding iterative resampling",99,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMSY10|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,9.963,1,0,1,0,0,0,1,Aptos|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,8.704,8.704,9.963,color,8,#C1E0EF|#B9C9B6|#81BE91|#7C8E60|#E6EDF1|#E4DBDC|#8CAB7F|#CEE6E6,0.5202,,,
iclr-2026-557a29cfb5fa,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,method,main,Figure 4,4,宽幅 denoising-loop 流程：batch、resampling、predicted clean sample、local feasibility、elite、repopulate。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|214.55,pipeline|qualitative_grid,2,3,1,"Figure 4: Compositional diffusion with Guided Search. At each denoising timestep, CDGS it- eratively denoises a batch of noisy candidate global plans by (i) iterative resampling to propagate information through averaged scores at overlaps (blue) and (ii) pruning candidates with local in- consistencies based on the predicted clean samples (yellow). This process ensures all local plans align and belong to high-likelihood regions of p(y), producing globally coherent plans.",69,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR10,9.963,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,CambriaMath|Aptos|Aptos-Bold|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,2.07,5.353,10.371,color,5,#DCEAF7|#FFF4D5|#56557D|#89A7B8|#E9CDA1,0.7785,,,
iclr-2026-557a29cfb5fa,ICLR,oral,replication_200,table,results,main,Table 1,7,OGBench PointMaze/AntMaze/Humanoid-Maze/Scene 的 success rate；100 trials、3 seeds，± 类型未命名。,double_column,90.00|270.22|522.00|521.66,table,1,2,1,"Table 1: OGbench [48]: learning from stitch and play datasets. With much less training data requirements, CDGS performs on-par with inverse-reinforcement learning baselines and better than generative baselines in a receding horizon control. For GSC, CD and CDGS, we replan based on distance from goal for maze tasks (following CD [40]) and sample the complete plan based on the oracle planning horizon for scene task. Success rate averaged over 100 trials and 3 seeds with randomly chosen task ids. Baseline performance is borrowed from original papers [48, 40]",88,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMSY10|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|NimbusMonL-Regu|CMMI10,4.592,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0147,,,
