iclr-2026-64b7228ce25e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 7,18,"Venn diagram for Shannon entropy, conditional entropy and mutual information.",double_column,90.00|255.56|522.00|562.44,conceptual_diagram,2,3,1,"Figure 7: A Venn diagram illustrating entropy, conditional entropy, and mutual information between the true state x and latent variable z. H(x) and H(z) denote the Shannon entropy (total information) of x and z, respectively. Their symmetric overlap, I(z;x), represents the mutual information that quantifies how much information about the true dynamics is preserved in the Koopman representa- tion. The non-overlapping regions, H(x|z) and H(z|x), correspond to the residual uncertainty not captured by I(z;x).",84,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMMI10|CMR10|CMSY10,9.963,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI10|CMR7|CMEX10,6.974,9.963,9.963,color,3,#FFEBEB|#B3FFB3|#C9EBB6,0.57,,,
iclr-2026-64b7228ce25e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 8,20,Autoregressive true-state and latent Koopman information flow.,double_column,90.00|33.54|522.00|340.42,map,1,2,1,"Figure 8: The autoregressive structure of Koopman representation. Top row (solid arrows): the original states x evolve under the nonlinear map T. Bottom row (dashed arrows): the states t−n are first encoded into latent variables z , which then evolve linearly under the Koopman operator t−n K. The latent variables are subsequently decoded back to approximate the original states. Thus, the latent evolution under Koopman representation captures essential structure but do not directly contain the full state information. Note: the dashed arrows represent the approximated Koopman representation in latent space, whereas the solid arrows denote the true underlying dynamics.",100,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI7|CMMI10,9.963,0,1,1,0,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMMI7|CMMI10|CMSY10|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMSY7,6.974,9.963,11.955,grayscale,0,,0.0017,,,
iclr-2026-64b7228ce25e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 9,26,Unit-circle versus contracting Koopman spectra under different regimes.,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|207.67,other,1,1,1,"Figure 9: Spectral behavior of the Koopman operator under different regimes. Left: Eigenvalues of K (orange dots) lie on the complex unit circle (|λ| = 1), and those of Kn with n = 7 (blue crosses) remain on the unit circle, indicating temporal coherence and preservation of information. Right: Eigenvalues of K lie strictly inside the complex unit circle (|λ| < 1), and the spectrum of Kn contracts toward the origin as n increases, reflecting fast mixing and information dissipation.",77,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMSY10|CMMI10|CMR10,9.963,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,9.963,9.963,color,8,#F3D590|#F7E4BA|#FAF0D8|#E0A211|#FBF4E4|#FAEDD2|#E8E8D8|#F4D899,0.3001,,,
