iclr-2026-6f113e6f8081,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Fig. 1,2,Framework: batch chunks → retriever similarity → in-batch attention → NTP/backprop,double_column,90.00|71.76|522.00|378.64,pipeline|qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"via Language Modeling, abbreviated as Revela. As illustrated in Fig. 1, Revela trains retrievers by simultaneously optimizing retrievers and LMs; different from conventional NTP, Revela learns the probability of a token given both the prefix in this sequence and all other sequences in the batch. Specifically, in addition to classical self-attention which restricts NTP to individual sequences, an in-batch attention mechanism enables sequences to attend to their neighbors in the same batch during language modeling. In this process, the retriever provides inter-sequence dependencies that modulate the in-batch attention weights, allowing it to be optimized with the LM during training. We split raw texts into chunks within each document and put these chunks into the same batch, motivated by the idea of hard negative samples in contrastive learning (Xiong et al., 2020).",131,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusMonL-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,TimesNewRomanPSMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|Georgia-Bold|TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT|Georgia|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,1.878,4.506,9.963,color,8,#E1D5E6|#F7CFC9|#D8E7FB|#FFF2CC|#A4838B|#DEB9A8|#A25D5C|#A6A7B7,0.4141,,,
iclr-2026-6f113e6f8081,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Fig. 2,4,Architecture and attention-map placement of self-attention and in-batch attention,double_column,90.00|20.00|511.87|200.14,matrix|architecture|qualitative_grid|map,1,3,1,"Output Probabilities Softmax Similarity Linear Matrix xN Feed Forward Document Layer Norm ... Embeddings ... As shown in Fig. 2, in Revela, the NTP for sequence i is conditioned not only on its own preceding context xi but also on every other Self-Attention <l document in the batch, {D } . Specifically, In-Batch Attention j j̸=i we introduce a new attention mechanism in the transformer blocks, i.e., in-batch attention Attention Map (§ 3.2), which is supported by a specific mask design (§ 3.4). The attentions are weighted by",86,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|Georgia|NimbusMonL-Regu|CMMI7|CMMI10,9.963,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMMI10|CMMI7|CMR10|NimbusMonL-Regu|CMSY10,6.974,9.963,11.955,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-6f113e6f8081,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Fig. 3,7,BRIGHT and BEIR mean nDCG@10 with baseline/API/compute groupings,double_column,90.00|371.18|522.00|678.06,other,1,1,1,"Revela demonstrates strong performance on complex retrieval. Fig. 3 (left) shows the av- erage nDCG@10 across the 12 BRIGHT subtasks. Despite being trained unsupervised on only 340K raw Wikipedia documents, Revela outperforms the supervised E5-Mistral-7B-Instruct as 3B",38,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusMonL-Bold|NimbusMonL-Regu,9.963,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|DejaVuSans|DejaVuSans-Bold|NimbusMonL-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,1.496,9.963,9.963,color,4,#1F77B4|#91B491|#8EA9BB|#CC9797,0.4288,,,
iclr-2026-6f113e6f8081,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,table,results,main,Table 1,7,"10-task CoIR main comparison across sparse, supervised, self-supervised and API models",inset,166.73|171.83|186.41|252.02,table,1,1,1,"Table 1: Performance on CoIR (nDCG@10, %). Gray indicates supervised models. Bold marks the highest score among non-API models in each row. Columns marked † used code-related pairs during pre-training. The results of APIs are collected from Li et al. (2025). Without query-document pairs, Revela surpasseslargersupervisedmodelsandproprietaryAPIs, averagedacross10tasks. 3B",47,7,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|NimbusMonL-Regu|CMSY7,9.963,1,0,1,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,6.974,6.974,6.974,grayscale,0,,0.0,10,1,1
