iclr-2026-7c24d2356ca5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,把 static dataset → reweighted dataset → conditional diffusion → target-conditioned designs 画成 offline training/sampling 两段端到端管线。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|287.01,pipeline|pareto,1,1,1,"Figure 1: Overview of the PCD framework, which reframes offline MOO as a conditional sampling problem. Training: A conditional diffusion model is trained on a static dataset, using a novel reweighting strategy to emphasize high-quality solutions near the Pareto front. Sampling: At inference, the model directly generates novel designs conditioned on target objectives. This end-to- end approach sidesteps the need for the explicit surrogate models and separate optimizers required by prior methods.",72,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,ArialMT|Arial-BoldMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,7.334,8.556,13.445,color,8,#83A8D4|#D6A665|#D0E2F4|#C9DAF6|#2B5892|#FFF2CD|#B2CBE3|#70788E,0.774,,,
iclr-2026-7c24d2356ca5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,5,三步展示 objective partition/ranking、direction assignment、extrapolation + Gaussian noise。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|201.21,pipeline|qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 2: Overview of the conditioning points generation procedure: a) The objective space is partitioned via direction vectors, and points are ranked based on non-dominated sorting. b) Each direction vector is paired with the point closest to it in perpendicular distance (black arrow). The rest of the points are paired to the vector with the least amount of assigned points (gray arrow). c) A diverse set of conditioning points is generated by extrapolating the assigned points along the direction vectors and adding Gaussian noise.",84,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,9.963,9.963,color,8,#E38270|#0000B2|#D5D3E4|#FE0000|#2E152A|#7B3B14|#DBEBFD|#CDAB90,0.0932,,,
