iclr-2026-82716d8e922b,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 1,2,跨栏对照 vanilla 与 T3 的 rollout generation、BTR entry 和 credit assignment。,double_column,90.00|20.00|523.25|255.26,pipeline,1,1,1,"Figure 1: Overall framework of T3, where (b ,a ,o ) denote the agent’s internal belief, its chosen t t t action, and the resulting feedback at turn t, respectively. By truncating belief-trapped trajectories, we prevent the agent from entering the belief-trap region (BTR) where credit assignment is contaminated in RL training, allowing learning signals to concentrate on genuinely informative actions. As a result, policy optimization becomes more stable and effective under complex active reasoning.",75,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMMI10|CMMI7|CMR10|CMBX10,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,TimesNewRomanPSMT|ComicSansMS|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|DengXian-Regular,4.664,4.664,9.963,color,8,#D8D2C4|#EABA95|#FFF3D0|#F9D5A8|#CE6A3E|#6FADB9|#5D6775|#81CDDF,0.406,,,
