iclr-2026-82716d8e922b,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 7,25,PE surrogate Ψ̂/ĉθ 的 lower-envelope binning 与线性 fit。,double_column,90.00|20.00|523.74|204.34,line|qualitative_grid,2,4,1,"Figure 7: Empirical visualization of Assumption 1 on the PE task. The dashed vertical line marks the empirically determined threshold Uˆ . Blue points show all samples, while orange points represent the 0 binned lower envelope, obtained by partitioning the range of {Ψˆ ≥ Uˆ } into equal-width bins and t 0 taking the 10th percentile of cˆ within each bin. The red line is a linear fit to these lower-envelope θ points. For (a), we empirically select Uˆ = 10, and obtain the linear fit: cˆ = 0.0969 × Ψˆ − 3.0478. 0 θ ˆ ˆ",92,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|CMMI10|CMSY10|CMR7,9.963,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,8.966,8.966,9.963,color,8,#1F77B4|#B5D1E4|#D8E7F1|#DDE9F2|#629CC6|#D1A487|#D5DFE8|#98606B,0.4099,,,
iclr-2026-82716d8e922b,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 8,25,PE/CD early-token GAE、tail length 和 CD truncation strength。,double_column,90.00|254.24|522.17|561.12,other,4,2,1,"Figure 8: Empirical verification of Theorem 2 and Corollary 1. (a-b) Without truncation, early-token advantages exhibit a clear negative drift, while T3 consistently elevates them across PE and CD tasks. (c) Longer uninformative tails (higher maximum interaction turns, from 6 to 15) cause stronger suppression of early advantages. (d) Stronger T3 truncation (smaller k) yields cleaner, less-biased early advantages.",59,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMBX10|CMBX7|CMMI10,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,DejaVuSans|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|CMMI10|CMSY10|CMR7,1.741,4.464,9.963,color,8,#FD9C4B|#4C92C2|#BB554E|#CAD1D5|#F7D7C1|#786D7F|#97C1C0|#C38477,0.252,,,
iclr-2026-82716d8e922b,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 9,26,成功 rollouts 的 artificial false-positive truncation 对 early GAE 的影响。,double_column,90.00|20.00|523.65|216.93,other,2,2,1,"Figure 9: Empirical verification of the effect of false positive on (a) PE and (b) CD tasks. More aggressive false-positive truncation (larger α) systematically reduces the advantages of early ex- ploratory actions, reflecting the removal of positive future return contributions.",40,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMMI10,9.963,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,DejaVuSans|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,1.741,4.464,9.963,color,8,#F7C6A8|#61B762|#FEA051|#E36860|#5E8AB4|#FDE6DB|#D5E7E3|#B1D9BB,0.208,,,
iclr-2026-82716d8e922b,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,table,appendix,appendix,Table 5,27,PE BinarySim threshold .85/.88/.90/.95 的 PPO/PPO+T3。,double_column,89.67|323.09|523.25|574.53,table,1,2,1,"Table 5 summarizes the results. Lower thresholds (e.g., below 0.80) cause the reward to activate (i.e., a 1 reward) almost continuously, which diminishes the discriminative value of high-quality predictions. Conversely, very high thresholds (e.g., above 0.95) make activations extremely rare, preventing PPO from learning effectively. Mid-range thresholds between 0.85 and 0.90 consistently yield stable training dynamics and strong downstream performance. We use 0.88, which lies within this empirically robust region, in the main experiments of the PE task.",86,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|CMMI10|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10|CMMI10|CMSY10|CMBX10,6.974,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0062,,,
