iclr-2026-82ba4792ed68,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,ablation,main,Figure 2,7,在 cora/arxiv/cornell 上比较 feature-edge deletion surfaces。,double_column,89.69|20.00|523.74|284.75,network,1,3,1,"Figure 2: Accuracy of 2-hop prompting and Graph-as-Code on the cora, arxiv, and cornell datasets under varying ratios of randomly removed edges and truncated text features. Table 3 suggests of a performance gap, with Prompting (ϕ ) performing worst and Graph-as-Code prompt best (Finding 4). In this setting, Prompting is constrained by node feature length and neighborhood size, both quickly exhausting the model’s token budget. Notably, similar token-limit issues appeared in previous sections—for the products dataset in short-text homophilic benchmarks and for the texas and washington datasets in the heterophilic regime when features were long or neighborhoods large.",99,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR10|CMMI10,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,9.963,9.963,color,8,#50C369|#229E86|#367075|#6ECD59|#3F3C78|#8ED54B|#A3D935|#E1E31D,0.9054,,,
iclr-2026-82ba4792ed68,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,ablation,main,Figure 3,8,在 photo 上显示 token-limit-driven divergence。,single_column,24.00|33.29|301.00|340.17,other,1,2,1,"Figure 3 shows that on photo we indeed observe a di- vergence in behavior between the two methods (Find- ing 7). This divergence on photo is expected given the dataset’s characteristics. Photo is highly homophilic and contains nodes with rich, lengthy feature descriptions. In homophilic graphs, nodes are densely connected to others of the same class, so 2-hop prompts accumulate a substan- tial amount of feature text from numerous neighbors. This quickly exceeds the LLM’s context window, leading to a",82,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMMI10,6.974,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
