iclr-2026-a8e7c788acec,ICLR,oral,replication_200,table,method,main,Table 1,3,"Two training stages, updated module and weights for Lconfidence, Ldiffusion and Lpairformer.",double_column,90.00|682.61|522.00|772.00,table,1,2,1,"tshteepbseahmapvliionrgoafndAfilpnhdaFthoaltdi3tsufnadileurrefepwri-- Table 1: Training stages and the weights of each term. marily arises from the sampling procedure itself. The default strategy of injecting extra stochastic noise and enlarging the ODE step size turns out to be detrimental in this regime: the enlarged step size significantly amplifies the bias in ODE predictions. To stabilize performance, we modify the sampler by disabling noise injection (setting the noise factor γ = 0), fixing the rescaling factor λ = 1, and normalizing the step size with η = 1, 0 thereby enabling stable one-step sampling. The first challenge concerns computational efficiency. After enabling one-step sampling, the Pair-",100,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|CMMI10|CMR7,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
