iclr-2026-ab553a040c74,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 8,14,"Traditional and recovered final-layer representations expose A-minus, Sigma, U, b, and canonical logits.",double_column,90.00|20.00|522.17|175.46,pipeline|map,1,2,1,"Figure 8: An overview of the intermediate representations in both traditional (gray) and our own (yellow) parameterization of the final LM layers. Representations (boxes) are annotated the functions that map between them (arrows), as well as the space in which they reside (blue tags). Our method recovers the parameters 𝚺, 𝑼, 𝒃, and 𝑨 , which in turn give us access to the cannonical − logit, ellipse, and rotated representations. Notably, the rotated representation that we recover is a pure rotation of the normalized representation.",83,4,TeXGyreTermesX-Regular|TeXGyreTermesX-Italic|NewTXBMI|txbmiaX|txsys,9.963,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,TeXGyreTermesX-Regular|txmiaX|NewTXMI5|NewTXBMI7|txsys|txbmiaX,5.479,5.978,9.963,color,7,#FFFDE9|#E6E6FF|#BCBAB0|#FFFDEC|#E4E2D7|#D5D4D1|#FAF8E4,0.2699,,,
iclr-2026-ab553a040c74,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 9,15,Layer norm output is the centered sphere-plane intersection; an isometry drops the centered axis.,double_column,89.64|20.00|522.00|156.87,conceptual_diagram|qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 9: An illustration of the layer norm output space (left), which is shown as the thick ring at the intersection of the plane perpendicular to 1 (due to centering) and a sphere (due to normalization). To reduce the dimension of the representation, we can apply an isometric transform that rotates 1 to align with an axis (right), then drop that axis.",62,2,TeXGyreTermesX-Regular|TeXGyreTermesX-Bold,9.963,0,0,1,1,0,0,2,TeXGyreTermesX-Regular|NewTXMI7|NewTXMI|txexs|txmiaX,7.273,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-ab553a040c74,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 10,16,Layer norm representation path from R^(d-1) sphere through ellipse and biased ellipse to canonical logits.,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|195.89,other,1,1,1,"Figure 10: Model representations and mappings between them for LMs with a layer norm. Compared to Figure 8, this model has an ellipse in 𝑑 1 dimensions. −",27,2,TeXGyreTermesX-Regular|NewTXMI|txsys,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,TeXGyreTermesX-Regular|txmiaX|NewTXMI5|NewTXBMI7|txsys|txbmiaX,5.479,6.476,9.963,color,8,#E6E6FF|#B7B7CB|#EFEFFF|#9999AB|#E8E8FF|#ECECFF|#CFCFE6|#DEDEF6,0.1207,,,
