iclr-2026-b7a66e10bf69,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,method,main,Figure 5,5,"RoSE pipeline from RGB and grayscale conversion through CLIP/VAE conditioning, video diffusion, shading sequence, and analytic solver; lock/fire icons distinguish frozen/trainable modules.",double_column,89.64|20.00|522.00|166.60,pipeline|architecture|qualitative_grid|image_montage|map,1,4,1,"Figure 5: Pipeline of RoSE. Given a monocular RGB image under arbitrary light, RoSE first converts it into a grayscale image, which is then used to generate the shading sequence via a video diffusion model. This generation is guided by two complementary feature representations extracted from a CLIP encoder and a VAE encoder. Finally, an ordinary least squares problem is solved analytically to estimate the normal map from the generated shading sequence. We train the video diffusion model while freezing the CLIP and the VAE encoder.",86,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,9.963,9.963,color,8,#F1B88C|#E6F1D6|#C5C9C6|#504F89|#6A93C5|#9C57A7|#81C7D6|#B69FAF,0.4038,,,
