iclr-2026-be5b1d259689,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,results,main,Figure 3,8,按 1–5 hop 展示模型 F1 随 reasoning chain length 的变化。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.17|221.01,qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,3,1,"Figure 3: Model F1 across samples with different Figure 4: Model ∆F1 vs. ∆ Step (difference in length chain lengths, showing a consistent drop in perfor- between generated and golden reasoning chains), where mance as the chain length increases. larger positive ∆steps indicate more over-retrieval. Topology-Specific Challenges. Across reasoning topologies, we observe Parallel Image-Text Fork is the most challenging, where all backbones reach their lowest F1 and HPS. The difficulty comes from the need to plan and cover both text and image branches simultaneously, so missing either branch directly lowers HPS, and under the top-1 retrieval constraint models often fail to capture the full evidence set. Aligning parallel evidence without strict order further increases the risk of incomplete or inconsistent reasoning. Multi-Images Fork is also difficult, mainly due to the challenge",130,7,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR9,9.963,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,DejaVuSans|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|HelveticaNeue-Bold,3.918,4.244,9.963,color,8,#B3D1E0|#FBE9E7|#FEF4EA|#C66E6A|#F7E9DB|#F6CFB2|#FCE5BD|#BFA39A,0.2882,,,
iclr-2026-be5b1d259689,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,results,main,Figure 4,8,展示 model delta F1 与 predicted/golden step-length difference 的关系。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.17|221.01,qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,3,1,"Figure 3: Model F1 across samples with different Figure 4: Model ∆F1 vs. ∆ Step (difference in length chain lengths, showing a consistent drop in perfor- between generated and golden reasoning chains), where mance as the chain length increases. larger positive ∆steps indicate more over-retrieval. Topology-Specific Challenges. Across reasoning topologies, we observe Parallel Image-Text Fork is the most challenging, where all backbones reach their lowest F1 and HPS. The difficulty comes from the need to plan and cover both text and image branches simultaneously, so missing either branch directly lowers HPS, and under the top-1 retrieval constraint models often fail to capture the full evidence set. Aligning parallel evidence without strict order further increases the risk of incomplete or inconsistent reasoning. Multi-Images Fork is also difficult, mainly due to the challenge",130,7,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR9,9.963,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,DejaVuSans|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|HelveticaNeue-Bold,3.918,4.244,9.963,color,8,#B3D1E0|#FBE9E7|#FEF4EA|#C66E6A|#F7E9DB|#F6CFB2|#FCE5BD|#BFA39A,0.2882,,,
iclr-2026-be5b1d259689,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,results,main,Figure 5,9,展示八类错误在样本中的比例。,double_column,89.69|20.00|523.75|227.07,other,1,2,1,"RQ5: Error Analysis. Figure 5 shows the distribution of eight error types, annotated using Gemini-2.5-Pro as the judge. The most frequent errors are Retrieval-Failure (84.7%), Hallucinated- Entity/Attribute (75.8%), and Step-Omission (74.3%), revealing that current models often fail to ground reasoning in relevant evidence, introduce unsupported content, or skip key steps. Mid-frequency errors (e.g., modality mis- match, spurious steps) reflect unstable plan- Retrieval-Failure 84.70% ning, while structural errors (order/depen- Hallucinated-Entity/Attribute 75.75%",80,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|DejaVuSans|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,0,1,1,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,7.807,7.807,9.963,color,8,#D4614B|#9AB3D3|#668CBD|#E29587|#F7E3E0|#DAE3EF|#DEBAB8|#DA7865,0.0794,,,
