iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Fig. 3,21,展示 no perturbation、paraphrasing、ADV paraphrasing 时 -log(p) 随 query 数的增长。,double_column,89.64|263.91|523.65|570.79,other,1,2,1,"signal used in our fingerprint detection. In Fig. 3, we show the detectability of our fingerprint under paraphrasing and adversarial paraphrasing with respect to the number of queries using LLAMA3.1- 8B. Compared to the baseline deployment, we see that both paraphraser indeed significantly lowers detectability, and that the adversarial paraphraser from Diaa et al. (2024) is very effective at removing the watermarking signal. Yet, as the number of queries increases, so does the detectability, and after ≈ 50 queries we can detect our fingerprint. This monotonous increase in fingerprint detectability with the number of queries is what enables the strong robustness of our fingerprint.",104,7,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|CMSY10,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR10|CMSY10|CMMI10,7.97,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0219,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Fig. 4,22,比较 semantic-conditioned 与 full watermark 经 Alpaca/Dolly/OpenMathInstruct finetuning 后的 detectability。,double_column,89.64|127.11|523.25|433.99,other,1,1,1,"Full Watermarking Is Less Robust Against Finetuning Fig. 4 shows that even non-adversarial finetuning (i.e., finetuning on a domain different from the one we use for detecting the fingerprint) significantly reduces detectability when using a full watermark instead of a semantically conditioned watermark. This means that, surprisingly, in addition to improving the stealthiness of the fingerprint, using semantically conditioned watermarks also contributes to the robustness of the fingerprint compared to full watermarking.",73,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|ArialMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|DejaVuSans|CMR10|CMSY10,1.79,9.963,9.963,color,8,#FFAEAE|#6784D4|#F2E5E5|#FF0000|#E5CDD0|#F18252|#F19264|#332BB1,0.0549,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Fig. 5,23,检验 completion-model fingerprint 在后续 instruction-tuning 后的 detectability。,unknown,,other,1,1,0,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,table,appendix,appendix,Table 6,23,比较 Qwen 2.5-3B fingerprint 前后在 GalicianBench/FrenchBench finetuneability 的 before/after accuracy。,single_column,311.00|418.79|588.00|670.23,table,1,1,1,Table 6: Evaluation of Our Fingerprint Impact on Finetune-,9,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10,7.97,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0222,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,ablation,main,Fig. 6,24,查询数消融：base、finetuned、paraphrased 三种状态的 -log(p) 随 |Q| 变化。,double_column,90.00|219.89|522.00|526.77,line,1,2,1,"Results Fig. 6 shows that detectability increases with the number of queries. For all three settings evaluated, we see that the fingerprint is detected with 100 queries already. This highlights the strength of using a statistical signal: even in cases where the signal is degraded, we can recover a strong fingerprint signal simply by scaling the number of queries. Moreover, the base model fingerprint detectability (orange line) is flat, showing that our fingerprint is principled and does not induce an abnormal false positive rate.",84,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10,9.963,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|ArialMT|CMR10|CMSY10|DejaVuSans,4.495,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0146,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,ablation,main,Fig. 7,25,比较三个 semantic domain 的 detectability/query scaling。,double_column,90.00|300.88|523.65|607.76,line,1,2,1,"Semantic Domains Should be High Entropy Fig. 7 shows that the detectability with respect to the number of queries scales differently across domains. This is because LLM watermark de- tectability (i.e., the detection power of the watermark) is bounded by the entropy of the LLM distribution (Kirchenbauer et al., 2023). Hence, the entropy of the underlying semantic domain is critical when choosing the domain. On the positive side, we see that for all evaluated domains increasing the number of queries indeed increases the fingerprint detectability.",86,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|ArialMT|CMR10|CMSY10|CMMI10,1.782,9.963,9.963,color,8,#FF6363|#9CAED3|#1515B1|#C2D6E1|#FD8E6C|#7A78D0|#F6E8E7|#F5B1A1,0.067,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,table,ablation,main,Table 7,25,比较 French、Medicine、Math semantic domains 的 FSR 与 8 个 benchmark accuracy。,single_column,161.11|225.02|411.37|361.38,table,1,1,1,"Table 7: Effectiveness of Our Fingerprinting Method On Different Semantic Domains We compare the Fingerprint Success Rate (FSR) of QWEN2.5-3B fingerprinted on three different domains. We also compare the utility, measured through benchmark accuracy, and report the average accuracy in the last column (AVG). We highlight in bold FSR values of 1.0.",54,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10|CMMI10,9.963,1,1,1,0,0,0,2,,,,,color,8,#E9E7E3|#90A6CB|#7CCAB2|#FC8C6B|#A3BED1|#AADDCD|#FF6363|#FD4647,0.7367,2,1,1
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,ablation,main,Fig. 8,26,展示 δ 对 detectability、PPL 和 FrenchBench accuracy 的 trade-off。,double_column,89.69|248.60|523.74|555.48,other,1,2,1,"Results Fig. 8 shows that increasing δ indeed significantly increases detectability, and that 1000 queries are enough to detect the fingerprint for all δ tested. The right side of Fig. 8 shows that, at the same time, increasing δ also slightly increases perplexity in the semantic domain. Similarly, increasing δ also slightly decreases FrenchBench accuracy (from 0.61 at δ = 0.5 to 0.57 at δ = 5). This means that, for the model provider, there is a trade-off between the cost of detectability (due to the increased number of queries needed to detect the watermark) and the impact on quality. Given that the impact on quality is minimal even with δ = 4 (see the benchmark results from Sec. 5.1) and limited to the semantic domain, we argue that detectability is more important and thus decided to use δ = 4 for our main experiments in Sec. 5",148,8,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR10|CMMI10|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10|CMMI10,6.642,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0009,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,table,ablation,main,Table 8,26,比较含／不含 Eq. (2) regularization 的 FSR 与 benchmark utility。,double_column,89.67|324.00|522.00|575.44,table,1,1,1,"Table 8: Effectiveness of Our Fingerprinting Method We compare the Fingerprint Success Rate (FSR) of our method with (Ours) and without the regularization (Ours (w/o)). We also compare the utility, measured through benchmark accuracy, and report the average accuracy in the last column (AVG). We highlight in bold FSR values above 80%.",53,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,1,1,0,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10|CMMI10,6.642,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0037,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,ablation,main,Fig. 9,27,在 Math、Medicine、Q&A、Code query 上检验 math fingerprint leakage。,double_column,89.50|313.56|522.00|620.44,other,1,1,1,"No Fingerprint Leakage Fig. 9 shows that there is no fingerprint leakage. Even when using 1000 queries for fingerprint detection, only the queries in the semantic domain, i.e., math, contain a detectable watermark signal. This means that, for a targeted adversary to detect the fingerprint (such as in Gloaguen et al. (2025a)), they would indeed need to know the semantic domain beforehand.",63,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10|CMSY10|CMMI10,7.97,9.963,9.963,color,8,#2A2AB8|#0202AA|#6F5ABA|#D1C7E5|#8F7EC9|#B3A5D7|#9C2A6C|#DFD9EE,0.0668,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Fig. 10,30,用 ROC 比较单 watermark token 与 opening/closing token trigger 的 TPR/FPR。,double_column,89.53|190.72|523.74|497.60,line|qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"In Fig. 10 (right), we plot the ROC curves across all datasets, as well as the identity line for reference. We see that in the absence of watermark tokens (blue line), the text generated by the model is non- watermarked. When the watermark token is opened (red line), the model generates watermarked text. Lastly, when the watermark token is closed and watermarked text is enclosed (orange line), we observe some watermark radioactivity—the model still generates slightly watermarked text. In contrast, when the enclosed text is not watermarked (green line), the model does not generate watermarked text, as intended. These results show how flexible semantically conditioned watermarking can be. Use cases for using opening and closing tokens as a trigger can include the watermarking of open-source reasoning models, where only the thinking trace or only the answer is watermarked, thus minimizing",141,7,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|BeraSansMono-Roman|ArialMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,4.672,9.963,9.963,color,8,#8A9396|#F98184|#FFD6D6|#FFE8E8|#FFA8A8|#FF9595|#B3BDC3|#FF8888,0.0693,,,
iclr-2026-c6856f20a2f5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Fig. 11,31,用多 detector ROC 检验最多 4 个 token-conditioned watermark keys 及跨 key 混合。,double_column,89.64|257.19|523.25|564.07,other,1,2,1,"Semantically Conditioned Watermarks Generalize to Multiple Keys In Fig. 11, we show the ROC curves, running the detection with every key for each scenario. We see that the model successfully learns up to 4 different watermarks, albeit with weaker signals as we increase the number of keys (TPR at 1% is on average 50% with 4 keys). Moreover, we see that even with the detector corresponding to another key (for instance, detector 1 with [WM2] instead of [WM0]), the detection rate is sometimes abnormally high. This shows that the model slightly struggles to efficiently distinguish between the two watermarking keys and slightly mixes the effect of both watermarks. Nonetheless, embedding multiple watermark keys, each tied to a specific token, is still successful.",122,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|ArialMT,1.105,9.963,9.963,color,8,#CC6B69|#D8957E|#8C979C|#BBCFCE|#88B09A|#E7BDB2|#E6E6E1|#E7D7D9,0.13,,,
