iclr-2026-d2112f671397,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 11,21,展示 blur level 与 foveal token count 对 CLIP、DreamSim 和 FID 的影响。,double_column,90.00|236.02|522.00|542.90,image_montage,1,2,1,Figure 11: Influence of blur-level and foveal token count on image generation quality. (Top Row) Image generation quality decreases as greater blur degrades the base image. (Bottom Row) Image generation quality increases as a function of increasing foveal tokens.,39,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,0,1,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|unknown|NimbusRomNo9L-MediItal,1.712,9.963,9.963,color,8,#34AE7A|#6BC39A|#F6697D|#F48C9E|#F6CDD4|#A2D7C2|#C5E6D7|#EBE9E9,0.2036,,,
iclr-2026-d2112f671397,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 12,22,比较 PSNR physical similarity 与 DreamSim semantic distance 对 same/different 的分辨能力。,double_column,90.00|20.12|522.00|327.00,qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,2,1,"Figure 12: Comparison of pixel-level (PSNR) and semantic (DreamSim) similarities in metameric judgments. (A, Left) portrays the histograms of PSNR values for generated images judgedas“same”or“different”inthebehavioraltask, withnearlyidenticaldistributionsbetweenthe two groups. (B, Right) shows the relationship between PSNR and DreamSim distances for all image pairs. There is a clear vertical separation by DreamSim distance that corresponds with metameric judgments, while PSNR values do not discriminate between what is considered metameric.",71,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,0,1,1,0,0,2,unknown|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,1.959,7.476,9.963,color,8,#FFD6FC|#F2DFFF|#DDB5A3|#644C55|#F2AC8C|#BECCD0|#FAC8CB|#B3B1A5,0.6528,,,
iclr-2026-d2112f671397,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 13,23,比较 full、peripheral-only、foveal-only stream 的 fooling rate 与生成样例。,double_column,90.00|42.55|522.00|349.43,qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,2,1,"Figure 13: Higher metameric (same) judgments for images incorporating both peripheral and foveal information. Using both foveal and peripheral features produced the highest fooling rates. Peripheral-only conditioning yielded the second best results, while foveal-only generations lagged significantly behind. Although the difference between peripheral-only and combined foveal- peripheral conditioning is small, it is meaningful: the additional high-resolution details from fixa- tions lead participants to be more easily fooled.",67,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,0,1,0,0,2,unknown,2.162,6.875,8.25,color,8,#C9D2E3|#F2C4E0|#FDC5B0|#5A3F3F|#776C61|#8C9D99|#DA9F8B|#77C4AF,0.6197,,,
iclr-2026-d2112f671397,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 14,24,展示三种 input visual streams 在层级、depth、mIoU、CLIP、DreamSim 上的相关结果。,double_column,90.00|270.44|522.00|577.32,tree,1,1,1,"Figure 14: Impact of input visual streams on hierarchical feature analyses. (Top Row) Multi- level feature analysis using neurally-grounded model (Jang & Tong, 2024) on driving metameric judgments. (Middle Row) Mid-level visual features driving metameric judgments (mid-level sege- mention mIoU and SiLog depth estimation). (Bottom Row) High-level visual features driving metameric judgments (CLIP cosine similarity and DreamSim distance).",57,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,1,0,0,0,2,unknown,1.864,4.268,7.114,color,8,#8C9FCA|#65C1A4|#FB8B62|#DFE7E1|#DCCCCE|#90A3CB|#E89D83|#8EBDBF,0.4017,,,
iclr-2026-d2112f671397,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 15,25,比较 DINOv2 与 CLIP vision encoder 的 FID 和 DreamSim quality curves。,double_column,90.00|301.78|522.00|608.66,architecture|image_montage,1,3,1,"Figure 15: FID and DreamSim evaluations based on DINOv2 and CLIP as vision encoders for foveal and peripheral feature extraction. (Left) The image generation quality (FID) for DINOv2- based peripheral generations is consistently better than CLIP patch embeddings. For DINOv2, we observe a sharp drop when decreasing the blur level, showing how decreasing blur results in the model encoding different, more accurate image features. This is not true for CLIP patch tokens, which seem to encode the same limited information across all blur levels. (Right) With increasing numbers of foveal token inputs, the DreamSim distance for both DINOv2 and CLIP-based embed- dings decreases. However, DINOv2-based generations yield greater semantic similarities with the original images, especially at low token counts.",119,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|unknown,1.874,9.963,9.963,color,8,#FB8C62|#F0EAE3|#64C1A4|#F29D7B|#FA8D63|#E6D3CA|#78C7AF|#F74872,0.1179,,,
iclr-2026-d2112f671397,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 16,26,展示不同 downsampling blur levels 下 DINOv2 与 CLIP 的视觉生成样例。,double_column,90.00|208.10|522.00|514.98,qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,3,1,"Figure 16: Image generation examples across blur levels using DINOv2 and CLIP as vision encoders. DINOv2-based peripheral generations resemble the original images more than CLIP- based generations, even at low blur levels. As the rate of downsampling decreases (28 × 28 → 448 × 448), DINOv2-based generations continue to show substantial improvements while CLIP- based generations exhibit minimal improvements. For the bottom two row pairs, DINOv2-based generations are able to keep the size of the plane (as well as its spatial position) intact irregardless of blur level input. However, that is not the case for the CLIP-based image generations.",96,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10|CMSY10,9.963,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,unknown,1.708,4.925,5.91,color,8,#9CADC0|#424235|#8DAAC7|#7C5854|#B4C1D2|#6C8FA7|#D0D6E2|#949194,0.6594,,,
iclr-2026-d548949c4ba4,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,同时展示一张 sparse matrix 对应多个候选 CUDA programs，以及 pretrained LM actor、critic、compiler/executor 与 correctness/time reward 的闭环。,double_column,90.00|318.94|522.35|625.82,matrix|pipeline|qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 1: An example task (Right): Each task is defined by a sparse matrix, which contains row and column indices of non-zero elements. The expected output is an SpMV program to be checked for functional correctness and execution efficiency. The input sparse matrix is the dynamic input at runtime and closely related to execution time. A high-level overview of our SparseRL method for sparse CUDA code generation (Left): we treat a pre-trained language model (LM) as a stochastic policy, code generation steps as actions, and rewards can be estimated based on the functional correctness and execution time of output programs from the compiler and executor (environment).",106,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,1,1,0,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|unknown|NimbusRomNo9L-MediItal,4.248,9.963,9.963,color,7,#CFE1F2|#7B6481|#F3BFC0|#B3C4CC|#D9E9D3|#A7A2AF|#809293,0.4017,,,
iclr-2026-d548949c4ba4,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,4,将 CUDA augmentation pre-training、Sparse Matrix→SpMV program SFT、actor/critic RL 与 reward 串成三阶段训练流程。,double_column,89.67|82.60|523.74|389.48,matrix|pipeline,3,4,1,"Figure 2: Overview of our method to optimize pretrained LMs for sparse CUDA code generation. (a) At pre-training stage, additional CUDA code is used to augment the LM. (b) At supervised fine- tuning (SFT) stage, the LM is finetuned for the Sparse CUDA code generation. (c) At RL stage, the actor and critic networks are first initialized from the finetuned LM, and then updated based on the reward of RL. The reward function is composed of correctness and efficiency rewards.",80,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|unknown,4.076,9.963,9.963,color,8,#D8E9D3|#CFE1F2|#F9F9E9|#F2E3CD|#C7C0B6|#BC5C5C|#F9F9CA|#CFDFCA,0.1901,,,
