iclr-2026-d8ed6882cb29,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 6,23,"Base Arena Elo versus safety-filtered Elo after flipping the top 1,000 anti-refusal examples.",double_column,90.00|254.84|522.00|561.72,qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 6: Elo, as computed using Chatbot Arena preferences, changes after re-labeling unsafe exam- ples. As in Figure 3a, we flip the labels of the examples with the largest 1000 values of a misaligned anti-refusal feature, and recompute Elo. We find that several models experience large shifts in Elo after adjusting these labels: in particular, the more recent models that perform better overall on Arena drop more Elo, suggesting that they refuse requests less often.",75,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|Inconsolatazi4-Regular,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,ArialMT,3.077,6.93,13.86,color,8,#FF5A5A|#5AAC5A|#F6D5D1|#FF6D6D|#5CAD5C|#95C895|#83655C|#C99B89,0.0507,,,
iclr-2026-d8ed6882cb29,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 7,24,Consistency of CA subjectivity `τj` estimates under REML/PM and full/half annotator pools.,double_column,90.00|202.60|522.00|509.48,other,1,2,1,"Figure 7: Computing τ subjectivity values using different methods yields highly-correlated results. j We compute τ using both restricted maximum likelihood (REML) and the Paule-Mandel (PM) j estimates across all 31 statistically significant features in CA, using all annotators with at least 200 annotations. We also randomly split the set of eligible annotators into two halves A and B, and recompute τ using only half of the annotators at a time. All of these different estimation procedures j yield τ estimates across the 31 features with high Spearman ρ and p < 0.001. j",94,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMMI10|CMR10|CMMI7|Inconsolatazi4-Regular,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,ArialMT|DejaVuSans,7.187,8.8,10.267,color,8,#FDE724|#D5E11A|#E5E318|#A8DB33|#CEDF1D|#67CC5C|#435845|#61B65E,0.862,,,
