iclr-2026-d930d9c23cc7,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 1,4,"Two-stage pipeline: select TAs/UAs from task property and output modality, then produce criterion-specific feedback and pair scores.",double_column,89.64|101.83|523.75|408.71,tree|pipeline|conceptual_diagram|qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,3,1,"Figure 1: An illustration of the evaluation pipeline. The pipeline consists of two steps: (1) Aspect Selection: First, appropriate aspects are selected from the TAs and UAs Trees based on task property and output modality. As illustrated, the question focuses on “cat image next to the orange dog picture”, while the image shows no cat adjacent to the orange dog. This discrepancy enables evaluation of the model’s ability to avoid hallucinations, specifically its performance on Context Inconsistency. Second, given the text output modality, aspects are selected from the Text Branch in the UAs Tree. (2) Evaluating: UFEval generates feedback and scores based on the input content and selected aspects.",110,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,,,,,color,8,#D6ECE9|#FBF1DF|#CDE6E6|#CAE5E4|#CAE3E3|#D5D1D0|#958D89|#EDEADE,0.393,,,
