iclr-2026-d99017a21fe7,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,theory,main,Figure 1,5,GSM8K 上 low-confidence/random remasking 与 suffix prompt 的首次正确答案出现分布。,double_column,90.00|49.95|522.00|356.83,line,4,3,1,"Figure 1: Distribution of early correct answer detection during decoding process.. Histograms show when correct answers first emerge during diffusion decoding, measured as percentage of total decoding steps, using LLaDA 8B on GSM8K. Red and orange dashed lines indicate 50% and 70% completion thresholds, with corresponding statistics showing substantial early convergence. Suffix prompting (b,d) dramatically accelerates convergence compared to standard prompting (a,c). This early convergence pattern demonstrates that correct answer tokens stabilize as top-1 candidates well before full decoding.",81,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusMonL-Regu,9.963,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|TimesNewRomanPSMT,2.356,6.779,8.966,color,8,#5B9BCB|#B1D3E7|#8CBEDD|#E7A36E|#405F7C|#F8EDDF|#8AA0B1|#F9D8B7,0.6732,,,
iclr-2026-d99017a21fe7,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,theory,main,Figure 2,6,GSM8K 单例全位置热图，比较答案 token 与 CoT token 的稳定时间。,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|268.68,heatmap|box|qualitative_grid,2,4,1,"Figure 2: Decoding dynamics across all positions based on maximum-probability predictions. Heatmaps track how the top-1 token changes at each position, if it is decoded at the current step, over the course of decoding. (a) Without our suffix prompts, correct answer tokens reach maxi- mum probability at step 119. (b) With our suffix prompts, this occurs earlier at step 88, showing that the model internally identifies correct answers well before the final output. Results are shown for LLaDA 8B solving problem index 700 from GSM8K under low-confidence decoding. Gray indicates positions where the top-1 prediction remains unchanged, orange marks positions where the prediction changes to a different token, blue denotes the step at which the corresponding y-axis position is actually decoded, and green box highlights the answer region where the correct answer",132,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusMonL-Regu,9.963,1,1,1,1,1,0,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|TimesNewRomanPSMT,6.734,8.966,9.963,color,8,#FF8C42|#FBC5A3|#FD9F63|#FCAF7E|#65AF8D|#F7EAE2|#FAD7C1|#F9E2D4,0.5746,,,
iclr-2026-d99017a21fe7,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 3,6,Full-step 与 Prophet early commit 的解码流程及冗余步数示意。,double_column,90.00|259.59|522.00|566.47,pipeline|conceptual_diagram|qualitative_grid,2,3,1,"Figure 3: An illustration of the Prophet’s early-commit-decoding mechanism. (a) Standard full-step decoding completes all predefined steps (e.g., 10 steps), incurring redundant computations after the answer has stabilized (at t=6). (b) Prophet dynamically monitors the model’s confidence (the “Con- fidence Gap”). It triggers an early commit decoding as soon as the answer converges, saving a sig- nificant portion of the decoding steps (in this case, 55%) without compromising the output quality.",75,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,0,0,1,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|Menlo-Regular|Helvetica-Bold|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|Tahoma-Bold|Helvetica-BoldOblique,4.848,9.963,9.963,color,8,#E1BEE7|#6BBD6E|#5E37AE|#F8C9C5|#F6BE99|#9E768D|#98D69C|#D0AFC3,0.2692,,,
