iclr-2026-db71b40c7495,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,Qwen2-VL-7B attention versus saliency maps for correct wallpaper and hallucinated blue; saliency shows structured versus collapsed output-context grounding.,double_column,89.64|37.85|523.74|344.73,qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 1: Attention vs. Saliency Maps for Correct and Hallucinated Tokens (Qwen2-VL-7B). Left (correct token wallpaper): Attention maps show no distinctive pattern, while our LVLMs- Saliency maps reveal strong, structured grounding to prior outputs. Right (hallucinated token blue): Attention maps remain visually similar, but saliency maps collapse, signaling loss of contextual dependency.",52,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,0,1,1,0,0,2,Calibri-Italic|TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT|TimesNewRomanPSMT|Calibri|TimesNewRomanPS-BoldItalicMT|Arial-Black,4.014,7.005,7.953,color,8,#E3F2D9|#683539|#EAADAE|#50AE7D|#86726E|#FCEBE8|#F9DED4|#A8E197,0.7043,,,
iclr-2026-db71b40c7495,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 2,3,"Qwen2-VL-7B output-token saliency patterns; correct wallpaper attends to recent outputs with distance decay, hallucinated blue collapses across prior outputs.",double_column,89.64|20.00|522.17|323.48,qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 2: Output Token Saliency Patterns in Qwen2-VL-7B. When generating a correct token (e.g., wallpaper), the current token assigns high saliency to recent output tokens, typically decaying with distance. In contrast, when generating a hallucinated token (e.g., blue), saliency toward all prior outputs collapses — signaling contextual disconnection.",49,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,9.963,9.963,color,8,#FACDBF|#FCE9E5|#FDF0EC|#87B1BD|#E2F1E7|#FDEDEA|#AF688D|#7FEF8E,0.3432,,,
