iclr-2026-dedfde9d7c99,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 13,28,FrozenLake VPRL optimal、non-optimal、invalid trajectory 分类与失败类型。,double_column,90.00|312.97|522.00|619.85,line|qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 13: Generated visual planning trajectories from VPRL on the FROZENLAKE test set. We illustrate three representative categories: optimal, non-optimal, and invalid cases. In non-optimal examples, the model occasionally enters local loops but still has the chance to make progress toward the goal, see the first and third trajectories. In invalid cases, despite a significant reduction in failure rate, VPRL still exhibits errors such as disappearing agents, contradictory actions (e.g., simultaneous left and right), or unrealistic teleportation.",78,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,1,0,0,0,2,Google-Sans-18pt,8.937,8.937,8.937,color,8,#67D5ED|#D7E6F2|#DFECF5|#D7ECF5|#E4EFF7|#E6F1F9|#E8F4FA|#DFF0F7,0.6583,,,
iclr-2026-dedfde9d7c99,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 14,29,Maze VPRL optimal、non-optimal、invalid traces，含穿墙案例。,double_column,89.64|317.19|523.25|624.07,line|qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 14: Generated visual planning trajectories from VPRL on the MAZE test set. We illustrate three representative categories: optimal, non-optimal, and invalid cases. In non-optimal examples, similar to FROZENLAKE, the model occasionally enters redundant loops but still progresses toward the goal. Invalid cases include maze-specific errors, such as the agent erroneously traversing through walls, violating the structural constraints of the environment. Notably, we observe that in the last invalid case, the agent is able to plan an optimal trajectory in subsequent steps.",82,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,MicrosoftYaHei-Bold,8.979,8.979,8.979,color,8,#D1E1D8|#388AB3|#067410|#85B7AB|#A04B36|#0A8405|#C9B7AB|#B18072,0.102,,,
