iclr-2026-df25bb895158,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 2,2,Visual attention maps showing spatial locality in LlamaGen-1.4B.,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|180.11,image_montage|map,1,2,1,"Figure 2: Visualization of attention maps in the LLAMAGEN-1.4B model. There is strong spatial locality, as the attention of a decoding token is concentrated on nearby spatial tokens. LLAMAGEN encodes images into 24 × 24 tokens, where a token that is 24 positions earlier in the attention map corresponds to the token directly above it in the 2D grid.",59,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMSY10,9.963,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|HelveticaNeue-Bold,5.692,9.963,9.963,color,8,#48522A|#7FAA96|#BFE1D8|#4A8457|#DAEBE8|#91D0BC|#50AB7D|#E7F5F8,0.2719,,,
iclr-2026-df25bb895158,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,method,main,Figure 3,3,Contrasts raster-order AR with flexible parallelized AR and separates context tokens from position query tokens.,double_column,90.00|20.00|523.24|168.87,qualitative_grid,2,3,1,"Figure 3: Raster Order vs. Flexible Parallelized Autoregressive Modeling. (a) In raster order, each token simultaneously provides context and predicts the next token, restricting flexibility and efficiency. (b) Our approach decouples these roles: previously generated tokens supply context, while position query tokens drive parallel generation at arbitrary target positions. This separation enables both flexible order and efficient parallelization.",58,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-MediItal,9.963,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,HelveticaNeue|HelveticaNeue-Italic|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,3.449,6.899,9.963,color,8,#91936D|#C4CE96|#D9CBB7|#A0A577|#C9B59A|#E3D7C3|#DDE0B1|#CED7A1,0.2683,,,
iclr-2026-df25bb895158,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,method,main,Figure 4,4,Shows Context Attention and Query Attention in the training mask.,single_column,311.00|20.00|588.00|86.13,conceptual_diagram,1,1,1,1 2 6 Figure 4: Illustration of the training attention Context mask. Context Attention allows subsequent tokens Attention to attend to the context tokens causally. Query Query,27,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|HelveticaNeue-Medium,9.963,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,,,,,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-df25bb895158,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,method,main,Figure 5,4,Shows fused inference masking for encoding generated tokens and decoding target queries.,single_column,311.00|20.00|588.00|245.74,conceptual_diagram|qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,2,1,"Figure 5: Illustration of the inference attention mask. Encoding with image tokens and Decoding with position query tokens can be fused into a single step. Taking step 2 in Figure 3 (b) as the example, it simultaneously encodes the previously generated image tokens 3, 5 to update the KV-cache and decodes the desired image tokens 1, 2 and 6 in parallel.",61,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,9.963,1,0,0,0,0,0,0,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI10|CMR7,6.974,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-df25bb895158,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,method,main,Figure 6,5,"Compares cache/attention arrangements of SAR/ARPG, RandAR, and LPD.",double_column,89.86|20.00|523.65|166.89,architecture|qualitative_grid,3,4,1,"Figure 6: Comparison with other methods. (a) Encoder–decoder approaches such as SAR and ARPG generate tokens independently, since query tokens contribute no key–value pairs. (b) Decoder- only methods like RANDAR rely on positional instruction tokens, but the causal mask reduces parallel generation to batched next-token prediction and forces instruction tokens to be cached, doubling memory. (c) In contrast, our method employs a specialized training mask that ensures mutual visibility among concurrently predicted tokens while caching only the generated tokens.",81,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,0,0,1,0,0,1,HelveticaNeue|HelveticaNeue-BoldItalic|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,3.932,6.74,9.963,color,8,#339D83|#FCB929|#408A72|#367660|#756556|#358E58|#84BBA6|#DCC78D,0.5903,,,
