iclr-2026-f448909bdd66,ICLR,oral,replication_200,table,ablation,main,Table 3,8,"RGB-VAE versus PE-Head encoding time, quality, and EPE.",double_column,90.00|574.61|522.00|772.00,table,1,1,1,"Track Representation. We compare Table 3: Comparing track representation methods. our sinusoidal position encoding with Our sinusoidal PE with learnable track head outperforms a learnable track head against the RGB RGB-VAE in both quality and efficiency, achieving 40× encoding strategy using a frozen VAE, faster encoding critical for real-time streaming. following prior work (Gu et al., 2025b), where each 2D track is assigned a Time DAVIS/Sora unique RGB color vector and placed Method (ms) PSNR SSIM LPIPS EPE",79,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10|CMMI10|CMMI7,6.974,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-f448909bdd66,ICLR,oral,replication_200,figure,ablation,main,Figure 6,9,"Sink/window effects on LPIPS, EPE, and temporal stability.",double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|189.98,image_montage,1,2,1,"Figure 6: Impact of Sparse Attention Patterns. Using longer clips (up to 241 frames) from the Sora subset, we ablate attention sink size and local window size in extrapolation scenarios. Having at least a single sink chunk is crucial, but more provides marginal benefit, while larger window sizes degrade performance as attending to long-past history allows errors to accumulate in context tokens.",62,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,9.963,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,TimesNewRomanPSMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,5.962,5.962,9.963,color,8,#AF534A|#D19B92|#C5D9D1|#6B9881|#CBB7BE|#A77984|#EBC5B8|#EDEAE1,0.1594,,,
iclr-2026-f448909bdd66,ICLR,oral,replication_200,table,ablation,main,Table 4,9,"Sora Extended quality, latency, and throughput under sparse-attention configurations.",double_column,90.00|619.08|522.00|772.00,table,1,1,1,"Table 4 and Figure 6(b,c) respectively. We denote our configuration as chunk-3, sink-1, window-1 (abbreviated c3s1w1), while sliding window approach used in Self Forcing is c3s0w6, attending to a maximum of 6 previous chunks without sink tokens, with unbounded RoPE positions that scale with temporal frame count. Although removing sink tokens (c3s0w1) yields marginal speed improvements, this comes at the cost of degraded long-term generation stability.",68,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusMonL-Regu,9.963,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMSY10,7.97,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
