iclr-2026-fac989b896c5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,"Raw data→ADP Action/Observation→OpenHands, SWE-Agent, and AgentLab SFT; boxes, colors, arrows, and examples encode the translation.",double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|247.87,line|pipeline|qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 1: Overview of the Agent Data Protocol (ADP). Raw data from diverse sources such as SWE- Gym are converted into a standardized ADP format. ADP unifies data into Trajectory objects, which include two core components: Actions (API action, code action, message action) and Observations (text observation, web observation), enabling seamless integration with various agent SFT formats. Example conversions show how heterogeneous raw data is normalized for training agentic models.",70,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,9.963,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,font000000002e84fdd3|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,4.95,4.95,9.963,color,8,#FFF2CC|#EAD1DC|#D8D2E9|#C0BDB3|#ACABA6|#CFE2F3|#D7C7BE|#7A777C,0.6863,,,
iclr-2026-fac989b896c5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,table,related_work,main,Table 1,3,"Lists 13 datasets by C/S/T/W variety, count, source, and note.",double_column,90.00|299.47|522.00|550.91,table,1,1,1,"Table 1: Overview of Existing Agent Training Datasets. C=Coding, S=Software Engineering, T=API/Tool Use, W=Web Browsing. Dataset Variety Count Source Note AgentInstruct(Zengetal.,2023) CTW 1.9K synthetic MixtureofBrowsing,Database,OS,etc. Code-Feedback(Zhengetal.,2024a) C 66.4K manual Codegenerationwithruntimefeedbackloops CodeActInstruct(Wangetal.,2024b) C 7.1K synthetic Codegenerationandtoolusewithexecution Go-Browse(Gandhi&Neubig,2025) W 9.5K rollout Structuredexplorationwebrollouts Mind2Web(Dengetal.,2023) W 1.0K manual Humanwebdemosonrealwebsites NebiusSWETrajectories S 13.4K rollout SWE-agent trajectories from Nebius relying",79,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,7.039,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,7.039,9.963,9.963,color,8,#FF8000|#1818FF|#D3DCF7|#8CB9D1|#208798|#FFB372|#FFD8B9|#FFECDD,0.0621,,,
iclr-2026-fac989b896c5,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,6,Contrasts many-to-many converter topology with a hub-and-spoke ADP topology and labels O(D×A) versus O(D+A).,double_column,90.00|20.00|522.00|205.43,pipeline,1,1,1,"Figure 2: ADP collapses many-to-many conversions into a hub-and-spoke pipeline. Left: With- out ADP, each of D-many datasets needs a custom Raw→SFT converter for each of A-many agentic formats (quadratic O(D × A) effort), causing duplicated code and efforts. Right: With ADP, each dataset is converted once (Raw→ADP) and each agent only requires one converter (ADP→SFT), yielding linear O(D+A) effort. New datasets or agents plug in immediately to the rest of ADP.",77,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI10|CMR10,9.963,1,1,1,0,0,0,2,font000000002e851fa6|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu,5.747,5.747,9.963,color,5,#EAD1DC|#FFF2CC|#CFE2F3|#CEC3C5|#92949B,0.6973,,,
