iclr-2026-fd78f005be2e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,abstract,main,Figure 1,1,xAR-L versus xAR-L+Neon qualitative ImageNet-256 comparison; frontloads FID 1.28→1.02 and 0.36% compute.,double_column,90.00|331.82|522.00|638.70,qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 1: Good to great: Neon’s state-of-the-art performance on ImageNet-256. Neon elevates a powerful baseline generative model (xAR-L, top row) to a new level of sharpness and realism (bottom row) with a simple post-hoc merge. This leap in quality, improving the Fréchet inception distance (FID) from 1.28 to a record-breaking 1.02, is accomplished with only 0.36% extra training compute.",63,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,8.966,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusMonL-Regu|NimbusSanL-Regu,2.322,9.963,9.963,color,8,#375830|#373C28|#74856D|#7CACAE|#497947|#765E47|#8C2A2B|#E0A840,0.3689,,,
iclr-2026-fd78f005be2e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,theory,main,Figure 2,4,2D Gaussian log-Wasserstein heatmap contrasting negative extrapolation and 4× real-data oracle improvement.,single_column,311.00|20.00|588.00|80.37,heatmap|qualitative_grid|map,1,2,1,"Figure 2: Neon’s key idea: synthetic degradation and real- data improvement point in opposite directions. This toy 2D Gaussian example plots as a heat map the log Wasserstein distance to the true data distribution p from the generative data modelG . Weseethatupdatingthemodel’sparameters θ(ws,wo) in the reverse of the direction they would be updated by fine- tuningonself-synthesizeddata(increasingws)achievessimilar",61,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMMI6|CMMI9|CMR6,8.966,1,0,0,1,0,0,1,,,,,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
iclr-2026-fd78f005be2e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 3,6,Minimum FID over w versus self-training budget B for EDM-VP CIFAR/FFHQ and Flow CIFAR at multiple |S|.,double_column,89.78|20.00|522.16|189.85,image_montage,1,2,1,"Figure 3: Neon consistently improves FID with minimal self-training overhead. Minimum FID (optimized over extrapolation strength w) vs. self-training budget B (millions of images seen during fine-tuning on S) for varying synthetic dataset sizes |S|, on EDM-VP (CIFAR-10/FFHQ-64) and flow matching (CIFAR-10). Optimal gains use B ≤ 3Mi (< 2% of base model training compute for EDM; < 3% for flow), confirming Neon’s efficiency. At B = 0, FID reflects the base model (no Neon).",73,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMSY9|CMR9|CMMI9,8.966,1,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR6|CMSY10|CMMI6|CMSY7,2.322,6.974,9.963,color,8,#BBC8D4|#8C84AE|#54B498|#E4856D|#E6318C|#EBDADC|#E95394|#EEB8A8,0.1912,,,
iclr-2026-fd78f005be2e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 4,7,"FID, precision, and recall versus negative extrapolation weight w for EDM-VP CIFAR at several B.",double_column,90.00|20.00|522.23|173.46,other,1,2,1,"Figure 4: Neon trades precision for recall, yielding net FID improvement. For the EDM-VP model trained on CIFAR-10, we plot the FID, precision, and recall vs. negative extrapolation strength w for various training budgets B. w = −1 corresponds to the model directly trained on synthetic data, i.e., θ Neon = θs. w = 0 corresponds to the base model, i.e., θ Neon = θr. w > 0 corresponds to the negative extrapolation regime where Neon demonstrates its improvement capability. In each case, |S| = 6k",82,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMMI9|CMR9|CMSY9,8.966,1,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR6|CMSY10|CMMI6|CMSY6|CMMI7,1.939,5.978,9.963,color,8,#C7D8DE|#79B1AF|#E9A979|#ECCEBC|#97D2C0|#D0BABB|#EDEFE7|#B57A66,0.2138,,,
iclr-2026-fd78f005be2e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 5,7,Minimum FID over w and CFG γ versus B for xAR-B/L and VAR-d16/d30 across resolutions.,double_column,89.78|35.43|522.15|342.31,other,1,1,1,"Figure 5: Neon consistently improves autoregressive models across architectures and resolutions. We plot the minimum FID (optimized over merge weight w and CFG scale γ) versus the fine-tuning budget B for various synthetic dataset sizes |S|. From left: xAR-B and xAR-L on ImageNet-256 (with xAR-L achieving a state-of-the-art 1.02 FID), VAR-d16 on ImageNet-256, and VAR-d30 on ImageNet-512.",58,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMSY9|CMMI9,8.966,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR6|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMMI6|CMSY10|CMMI9,1.939,8.966,9.963,color,8,#BECED7|#699CA6|#ECC4B4|#E63D91|#E27150|#DF9B83|#79C4AE|#EEEDE7,0.1847,,,
iclr-2026-fd78f005be2e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 6,8,VAR-d16 FID/precision/recall heatmaps and asymptotic precision–recall curves over w and γ.,double_column,89.68|20.00|523.25|172.69,other,1,1,1,"Figure 6: Optimal precision-recall trade-offs for VAR-d16 as a function of w and γ. Left: Heatmaps for FID, precision, and recall on ImageNet-256 (|S|=750k, B=1.25Mi) from a grid search over w and γ. The star marks the best FID (w∗≈1.0,γ∗≈2.7) achieving FID 2.01, unreachable by either parameter alone. Right: Asymptotic precision-recall curves showing expanded behavioral range through joint tuning.",68,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR9|CMMI9|CMSY9,8.966,1,0,1,1,0,0,2,DejaVuSerif|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR5|CMR10|CMMI10|Cmmi10,2.253,2.435,9.963,color,8,#97172C|#25578A|#C4D9E2|#70A1BE|#EEA786|#281F47|#F8D3BB|#F9E6DA,0.6929,,,
iclr-2026-fd78f005be2e,ICLR,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 7,8,"Minimum FID versus B for IMM at T=1,2,4,8 and multiple synthetic-set sizes.",double_column,89.70|40.39|523.12|347.27,qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 7: Neon dramatically improves few-step inference for IMM on ImageNet-256. Minimum FID (optimized over w and γ) vs. fine-tuning budget B for different |S|. Synthetic data were generated using T=8, γ=1.5. From left: T=1,2,4,8 inference steps. Neon achieves substantial FID reductions with near-zero additional compute (< 0.005% of IMM’s training), with Neon improved model with 4-step nearly matching base model with 8-step generation quality.",73,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR9|CMMI9|CMSY9,8.966,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|DejaVuSerif|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR6|CMR5|CMR10,2.253,6.974,9.963,color,8,#A11D36|#EFAC8C|#B9D7E1|#3F5E8D|#79A2B3|#282148|#DB7356|#F6D5C1,0.5202,,,
