icml-2026-159ec0c7baad,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,3,Cross-column pipeline of EAP temporal fusion and I2O inference/pruning streams with shared memory.,page_width,36.89|20.00|560.04|315.22,pipeline,2,2,1,"Figure 2. Overall pipeline of EcoVLA. (a) Environment-aware Adaptive Pruning (EAP): EAP is a lightweight, environment-aware method that identifies sparsity variations by perceiving real-time dynamics. Considering the temporal consistency of VLA execution in physical environments, EAP integrates instantaneous features with historical features to jointly compute the sparsity pattern. (b) Interleaved Inference Orchestration (I2O): I2O interleaves sparsity pattern computation into the inherent FLOPs bubbles within the VLA inference using a non-blocking parallel paradigm.",72,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,8.966,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|DejaVuMathTeXGyre-Regular|TimesNewRomanPSMT|HYQiHei-EES|TimesNewRomanPS-BoldItalicMT,3.083,5.692,8.966,color,8,#FFEFEF|#493327|#FDEFC4|#EAE9DB|#F1D5C0|#F2F0E0|#C6CBC3|#867153,0.5761,,,
