icml-2026-2d22f08859e8,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,3,"Cross-column system diagram links data preparation, agent initialization, and the multi-agent loop.",page_width,36.89|20.00|559.76|303.02,pipeline|conceptual_diagram,1,2,1,"Figure 2. The ClinEdu Framework for simulating clinical ward rounds. The system begins with Data Preparation, where a medical case is decomposed into Socratic Steps. During Agent Initialization, the system matches an objective Patient Script with a subjective persona to create a Personalized Patient, while assembling a Student Team with diverse backgrounds and knowledge gaps. The Multi-Agent Simulation unfolds in a closed-loop cycle: (1) Students independently report their clinical analysis; (2) the Tutor generates Socratic guidance based on an internal thinking process; (3) the Specialist and Safety Supervisor perform a dual-filter review for factual accuracy and professional ethics; and (4) Students formulate actions to query the Patient or seek expertise from the Specialist.",113,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,8.966,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,TimesNewRomanPSMT|TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT|TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|Aptos-Bold|Aptos-Italic,2.411,5.207,9.71,color,8,#3F708E|#EDD4E2|#DDF2E1|#C2E6F5|#6599AB|#C9EDFB|#435173|#B4BBC3,0.5199,,,
