icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,abstract,main,Figure 1,1,标题页架构概览，展示 dWorldEval 的 controllability、consistency 和 progress scoring 定位。,page_width,52.87|95.05|559.48|401.93,architecture,1,1,1,"Figure 1 dWorldEval is a discrete diffusion world model designed to be controllable and consistent for reliable policy evaluation. It ensures action controllability and spatiotemporal consistency while providing the policy compatibility and faithful progress scoring necessary for accurate, automated policy ranking.",41,2,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold,8.966,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,ByteSans-Medium|CMR8|SFRM1000|CMR7|SFRM1200,6.974,11.457,16.937,color,8,#A88595|#C0A7A4|#918491|#4F506D|#956B80|#CBDDEE|#C2C5D1|#A29FA3,0.2606,,,
icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,3,总览 unified architecture、sparse keyframe memory 和 discrete progress token 三个组件。,page_width,52.87|20.00|560.42|300.63,pipeline|architecture,3,2,1,"Figure2 OverviewofdWorldEval. (a)Unifiedarchitecture: Diverse modalities are flattened into a single sequence, enabling the model to treat visual, control, and semantic tokens uniformly. (b)Sparsekeyframememory: A history of low-resolution keyframes is used to anchor global spatiotemporal consistency. (c) Discrete progress token: The model jointly predicts visual outcomes and discrete progress tokens to enable automatic success detection.",56,4,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold,8.966,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,,,,,color,8,#DAE3F3|#B4B19E|#FDEEB9|#9A776F|#F9E7E7|#C2D4C6|#E6F2E7|#E8D5BA,0.6159,,,
icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,experimental_design,main,Figure 3,4,展示 AgileX 双臂平台、三同步相机和 Clean the Table 的成功/失败 rollout。,page_width,52.87|20.00|559.14|220.41,qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,2,1,Figure 3 Real-world setup and rollout visualization. Left: The bimanual AgileX platform equipped with three synchronized cameras. Right: Result of a failure and a success rollout generated for the Clean the Table task; the insets in the top corners of each frame display the synchronized wrist views.,47,3,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold|SFTI0900,8.966,0,1,1,0,0,0,2,,,,,color,8,#928B8E|#48474B|#D2C5BD|#E2CBC3|#C3A19E|#EADED6|#AD4354|#B4B7B1,0.2362,,,
icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 4,6,在 RoboTwin 中并列 ground-truth simulator rollout 与 dWorldEval multi-view prediction，含 suboptimal/successful action。,page_width,52.87|20.00|560.67|228.08,qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,2,1,"Figure 4 Visualization of ground-truth vs. generated multi-view rollouts on RoboTwin [30]. Left/Right: subop- timal vs. successful execution. Top/Bottom: ground-truth simulator rollout vs. dWorldEval prediction, conditioned on identical action sequences. Each sequence displays the initial state followed by synchronized future frames.",43,7,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold,8.966,0,0,1,0,0,0,1,,,,,color,8,#2E414C|#C5B2CC|#547AB8|#C8D3D0|#ADA3C4|#A4B0C7|#E5DEDC|#3B5873,0.229,,,
icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,table,results,main,Table 1,6,LIBERO expert/failure 子集上的 LPIPS 与 ∆LPIPS action controllability 对照。,page_width,52.59|360.76|560.68|612.20,table,1,2,1,"Table 1 Action controllability on LIBERO [23]. Com- Table 2 Long-horizon consistency analysis. We re- parison of LPIPS vs. our dynamic-aware ∆LPIPS on port the round-trip LPIPS (↓) error, averaged across all Expert (D ) and Failure (D ) subsets. Baselines de- synchronized views, over varying horizons H. Without succ fail grade on failure data, while ours remains robust. memory, the model suffers from progressive drift; with memory, spatiotemporal consistency is effectively pre- LPIPS ∆LPIPS (↓) served even at H = 20. Method (↓) Expert Failure Action Horizon (H)",83,7,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold|SFCC0900|SFRM0600|CMR9,8.966,1,1,0,1,1,0,3,SFRM1000|ByteSans-Bold|SFCC0900|CMR10|SFTI1000|CMMI10,6.974,9.963,10.959,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,table,ablation,main,Table 2,6,Full 与 w/o Memory 在 H=5/10/15/20 round-trip 的 LPIPS consistency 对照。,page_width,52.59|360.76|560.68|612.20,table,1,2,1,"Table 1 Action controllability on LIBERO [23]. Com- Table 2 Long-horizon consistency analysis. We re- parison of LPIPS vs. our dynamic-aware ∆LPIPS on port the round-trip LPIPS (↓) error, averaged across all Expert (D ) and Failure (D ) subsets. Baselines de- synchronized views, over varying horizons H. Without succ fail grade on failure data, while ours remains robust. memory, the model suffers from progressive drift; with memory, spatiotemporal consistency is effectively pre- LPIPS ∆LPIPS (↓) served even at H = 20. Method (↓) Expert Failure Action Horizon (H)",83,7,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold|SFCC0900|SFRM0600|CMR9,8.966,1,1,0,1,1,0,3,SFRM1000|ByteSans-Bold|SFCC0900|CMR10|SFTI1000|CMMI10,6.974,9.963,10.959,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,ablation,main,Figure 5,7,(a) suboptimal action controllability 定性案例；(b) reversible round-trip 的 memory ablation drift。,page_width,52.87|20.00|560.41|296.11,line|qualitative_grid,2,4,1,"Figure 5 (a) Action-controllability under suboptimal inputs. We condition all methods on an unseen action sequence and compare their rollouts. While WorldGym [20] self-corrects the missed grasp into a successful pickup and WorldEval [20] hallucinates non-existent objects, Ctrl-World [10] fails to align with the input actions. In contrast, dWorldEval faithfully reproduces the failure. (b) Long-horizon round-trip consistency. We apply a reversible action trajectory: forward actions up to t = H∆, followed by the corresponding inverse actions to t = 2H∆. The full model returns close to the initial observation at t = 0, whereas removing history causes accumulated drift over the round trip.",100,7,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold|CMR9|CMMI9,8.966,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,,,,,color,8,#AE9E8F|#94867A|#BDB0A5|#A2978A|#7B5451|#B1A69C|#B9AC9F|#BCB9AF,0.3774,,,
icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 6,8,展示联合 observation/progress generation，以及 π0 checkpoints 上 Real、Human imag.、Auto imag. success rate。,page_width,52.87|20.00|559.48|169.47,qualitative_grid,2,4,1,"Figure 6 Joint generation enables automatic policy scoring. (a) At each rollout step, the world model jointly predicts the future observation oˆ and a scalar progress score vˆ ∈ [0,1], which finally indicates task success or t+∆ t+∆ failure. (b) Success rate estimates across checkpoints of a base policy π 0 [4] on three LIBERO [23] suites. We compare ground-truth execution (Real) against evaluations on generated rollouts: human judgment based on the generated observations (Human) and automatic evaluation determined by the model’s predicted progress score (Auto).",87,4,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold|SFTI0900|CMR9|CMR6,8.966,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,,,,,color,8,#A09284|#B0A191|#E5D8D6|#BBAC9B|#BDB2A4|#87716A|#B8A493|#CDB49E,0.3781,,,
icml-2026-315bbaf35118,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 7,8,scatter plot 对比 real execution 与 generated success rate，报告 Pearson r 与 MMRV。,page_width,51.79|85.55|560.42|392.43,scatter|qualitative_grid|image_montage,4,4,1,"Figure 7 Correlation between real-execution and world-model success rates. Scatter plots compare real success rates (x-axis) against generated estimates (y-axis), reporting Pearson correlation r and rank-violation MMRV (lower is better). (a) Comparison with video diffusion baselines (WorldEval [20], WorldGym [33] and Ctrl-World [10]) on LIBERO [23] (Single-view). (b-d) Ablation studies comparing dWorldEval against its w/o-history variant across diverse settings: (b) LIBERO (Multi-view), (c) Robotwin [30] with heterogeneous policies (π 0 [4], DexVLA [41], DP [6]), and (d) Real-world tasks. dWorldEval consistently achieves superior correlation and ranking accuracy across all domains.",91,5,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold|SFTI0900|SFCC0900|CMMI9,8.966,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold|SFTI0900|CMR9|CMR6|CMMI9,5.978,8.966,8.966,color,8,#B0A191|#9D8F87|#E3D8CF|#BBAB99|#BEB3A6|#A2B4BB|#826F75|#BEA38B,0.2133,,,
