icml-2026-42cbf99e9181,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 11,20,Shows R2 VPO and PPO learning curves for ten continuous-control tasks.,page_width,36.89|296.11|559.44|602.99,line,1,1,1,"Figure 11. Learning curves on DeepMind Control Suite tasks. The x-axis denotes the number of environment steps, and the y-axis represents the average episode reward. Solid lines denote the mean performance over 5 independent training runs with different random seeds, and shaded regions denote standard deviation. R2VPO (ours) consistently achieves higher returns and faster convergence compared to PPO.",58,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR9|CMR6,8.966,0,0,1,1,1,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|DejaVuSans|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusMonL-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR7,2.472,8.966,9.963,color,8,#466B90|#D1E0E9|#FFDFC3|#214261|#2D5175|#F0CCAB|#FFDEC1|#FFE6D0,0.3949,,,
icml-2026-42cbf99e9181,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 12,21,Compares stabilized R2 VPO and PPO on Dog-Run and Humanoid-Run.,page_width,36.89|32.64|559.59|339.52,other,1,1,1,"Figure 12. High-Dimensional Control with Stabilized Training. We compare R2VPO and PPO on Dog-Run and Humanoid-Run under a WPO-inspired stabilization setup. R2VPO achieves stronger performance than PPO on both tasks, while the later-stage decrease on Dog-Run suggests that this environment is sensitive to task-specific stabilization and regularization.",47,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR6,8.966,1,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|DejaVuSans|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|Cmr10|CMR7,2.378,9.963,9.963,color,8,#F7E1CE|#E0ECF5|#B6A696|#F6DECA|#F9E6D6|#E2D8CF|#F7E1CD|#F7E1CF,0.387,,,
icml-2026-42cbf99e9181,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,table,appendix,appendix,Table 5,21,"Reports runtime ranges for 1B, 4B and 7B/8B scales.",page_width,36.94|577.37|559.45|772.00,table,1,1,1,"Table 5. Average Training Runtime per Training Step. Comparison of wall-clock times across different model scales on 2 Huawei Ascend Atlas A3 nodes. R2VPO-ON maintains parity with standard baselines, while R2VPO-OFF incurs a modest increase due to multiple updates per data batch (UTD=2).",44,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR6,8.966,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR7|CMSY10,6.974,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
icml-2026-447e2cef4c1c,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,Contrasts Think–Answer monolithic thinking with PLANTAIN plan-level reject/accept and rewind; plan is the early intervention unit.,page_width,44.36|20.00|551.13|261.86,qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 1 | PLANTAIN Rewind-and-Repeat After post-training an interleaved reasoning model, we apply an iterative rejection-sampling strategy for inference-time plan guidance. PLANTAIN first produces a plan as its initial intermediate response. This plan is evaluated by a human judge or an LLM autorater. If accepted, the model proceeds to generate the final answer. If rejected, the process is rewound such that the rejected plan is appended to a history of failures, and the model is re-prompted to produce a new, distinct plan. Crucially, the response generated by PLANTAIN is typically of higher quality than the response produced by a standard Think–Answer model. Additionally, subsequent thinking blocks after a rejection plan are short because the model only needs to adjust the plan rather than regenerate full reasoning. This leads to early pruning of suboptimal reasoning paths and closer",137,7,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Bold|XCharter-Italic|txsys,10.909,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,XCharter-Roman,7.97,7.97,7.97,color,8,#8AB4F8|#FABC5D|#76C789|#744644|#E6E5B8|#FBD670|#877267|#6DA3BA,0.3485,,,
icml-2026-447e2cef4c1c,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,table,results,main,Table 1,9,"Compares No Thinking, Think-Answer, and Plan-Answer on P@1 and TTFR for two Qwen3 sizes and four tasks.",page_width,44.03|494.02|550.92|761.42,table,1,1,1,"Table 1 | Interleaved reasoning generalizes beyond coding tasks, reducing latency and preserving accuracy. Plan-first decoding (Plan-Answer) substantially lowers time-to-first-response (TTFR) while maintaining or improving pass@1 accuracy compared to the standard Think-Answer baseline with a token budget of 4096. Despite being post-trained only on coding data, the learned interleaved behavior transfers effectively to math, text-to-SQL, and reading comprehension tasks.",59,3,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Bold|XCharter-Italic|txsys,10.909,1,0,0,1,0,0,1,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Bold|txsys|XCharterMathMI|XCharter-Italic,10.036,10.909,10.909,grayscale,0,,0.0017,,,
icml-2026-447e2cef4c1c,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,table,results,main,Table 2,10,"Compares Plan-Answer, answer-level R&R, Best-of-N(5), and plan-level R&R on P@1 and TTFR.",single_column,198.10|350.23|449.64|388.24,table,1,1,1,"Table 2 | Inference-time strategies: Plan-level feedback provides earlier and more informative supervision than answer-level feedback, yielding higher accuracy and lower TTFR. Both Best-of-N and R&R (Plan) improve over the base Plan-Answer decoding without additional training.",36,2,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Bold|txsys,10.909,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,XCharter-Roman|txsys,9.963,9.963,9.963,grayscale,0,,0.0,1,4,1
icml-2026-447e2cef4c1c,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,table,ablation,main,Table 3,10,"Varying context window from 4096 to 8192 tests token-budget scaling for TA, Plan-Answer, and R&R Plan.",page_width,44.03|521.17|552.43|788.58,table,1,1,1,"Table 3 | Token-budget ablation: Interleaved inference achieves near-saturated accuracy at 4K tokens, highlighting efficient use of available context. While Think-Answer continues to improve with longer reasoning—reflecting redundant token usage—Plan-Answer benefits modestly from larger budgets but remains below Rewind-and-Repeat, indicating stable yet non-adaptive scaling. Rewind-and-Repeat achieves the strongest token efficiency and overall accuracy.",54,3,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Bold|txsys,10.909,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Italic,7.97,10.909,10.909,grayscale,0,,0.0035,,,
icml-2026-447e2cef4c1c,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,table,ablation,main,Table 4,11,"Reports prompts needing rewind, first/second approval rates, and Rewounded P@1.",page_width,44.03|287.05|550.91|554.45,table,1,1,1,"Table 4 | Rewind statistics. Fraction of prompts requiring plan rewinds and corresponding approval rates. On average, only 22% of plans require a rewind, and over 80% of corrections succeed within two attempts, demonstrating the efficiency of plan-level R&R.",39,3,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Bold|txsys,10.909,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Bold|XCharter-Italic|txsys,10.909,10.909,12.951,grayscale,0,,0.0016,,,
