icml-2026-57d6cc1a187d,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 7,21,比较两数据集的 cross-motion top-100 overlap。,page_width,43.20|20.00|552.30|301.15,qualitative_grid|image_montage,2,4,1,"Figure 7: Cross-motion influence overlap across datasets. Heatmaps showing the percentage overlap of top-100 influential training samples across motion categories for (a) 4DNEX and (b) VIDGEN datasets. Each cell (𝑖,𝑗) shows the percentage of motion category 𝑖’s influential data (aggregated from 5 queries per category) that also appears in motion category 𝑗’s top-100 influential samples. The asymmetric nature of the matrices (e.g., bounce→float ̸= float→bounce) arises because different motion categories have different numbers of unique influential videos, leading to directional overlap percentages. Consistent high-overlap pairs (e.g., bounce-float: 44.4%/46.3%) and low-overlap pairs (e.g., free fall-stretch: 12.8%/12.7%) across datasets validate that these influence patterns reflect fundamental aspects of motion representation in video generation models.",125,5,XCharter-Roman|XCharter-Bold|CMR10|CMMI10|CMSY10,9.963,1,1,1,1,0,0,3,DejaVuSans-Bold|XCharter-Roman|DejaVuSans,1.702,3.86,8.966,color,8,#C9ED97|#5D8A13|#D8F1B1|#DEF5BC|#F2FBE4|#EFFAE0|#F5FCEA|#E4F6CA,0.7539,,,
