icml-2026-5cb9c5807bca,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 7,16,Normalized primary-minor and tie co-occurrence matrices.,page_width,36.89|20.00|560.56|283.70,matrix,1,2,1,"Figure 7. Co-occurrence structures induced by annotator disagreement. Left: normalized primary–minor co-occurrence matrix C˜pm, capturing systematic minor emotions that co-exist with perceived primary affect (multiplicity). Right: normalized tie co-occurrence matrix C˜tie, characterizing high-confusion emotion pairs that frequently emerge as top-vote ties. Both matrices are computed over the 8-way label space and provide pair-level scheduling signals for Phase-2 verification, rather than admissible evidence for final adjudication.",68,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR6|CMBX9,8.966,0,0,1,0,0,0,1,DejaVuSans|DejaVuSans-Bold|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|DejaVuSans-Oblique,1.774,4.423,8.966,color,8,#FFFFCC|#FB9F48|#EC2E22|#DF171C|#B20C21|#E46E3B|#FBD387|#FFFFC9,0.8683,,,
