icml-2026-5cb9c5807bca,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 9,25,IEMOCAP primary-label distribution and annotator agreement.,page_width,36.89|20.00|559.44|265.92,other,2,2,1,"Figure 9. IEMOCAP label statistics under plurality voting. (a) Primary emotion distribution. (b) Annotator agreement level (Full consensus: 3-0; Majority: 2-1; Tie: 1-1-1). N=10,039 utterances with 3 annotators per utterance.",32,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR9|CMMI9,8.966,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,DejaVuSerif|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|DejaVuSerif-Bold|DejaVuSerif-Italic,2.761,6.106,8.966,color,8,#F18F01|#2E86AB|#C73E1D|#A93B61|#94B376|#4B425E|#F18F03|#F5B250,0.6324,,,
icml-2026-5cb9c5807bca,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 10,27,Phase-1 system prompt.,page_width,36.89|338.69|559.44|645.57,other,1,1,1,"Figure 10. System prompt for Phase 1 (Global Perception). The prompt instructs the agent to operate in a high-recall, intuition-driven mode, explicitly discouraging single-label predictions and encouraging the preservation of competing hypotheses, minor emotions, and tie cases. Strict label constraints are enforced to prevent taxonomy drift, while confidence ranking (high / mid / low) provides a coarse uncertainty signal for downstream evidence verification.",61,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,8.966,0,0,0,0,1,0,1,font000000002f29c981,6.984,6.984,6.984,color,8,#F1F9E5|#77A461|#ACC99A|#EFF7E3|#DAE8CC|#F5FCE9|#F0F9E4|#F2F9E6,0.9677,,,
icml-2026-5cb9c5807bca,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 11,28,Phase-2 system prompt.,page_width,36.89|333.71|559.59|640.59,other,1,1,1,"Figure 11. System prompt for Phase 2 (Evidence Verification). The prompt instantiates the agent as an evidence-seeking investigator operating under the Explicit Information Retrieval (EIR) constraint. The agent is instructed to resolve ambiguity by selectively invoking structured semantic, acoustic, and refinement tools, reasoning only over retrieved observations rather than latent representations. This phase supports adaptive, hypothesis-driven evidence accumulation while explicitly discouraging unsupported intuition or premature adjudication.",66,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,8.966,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,font000000002f2a69e1,6.107,6.107,6.984,color,8,#F9F1D9|#E2BE8F|#FBF5DF|#D09756|#F8EFD7|#F1DFBF|#F9F1DA|#F9F1D8,0.975,,,
icml-2026-5cb9c5807bca,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 12,29,Phase-3 system prompt.,page_width,36.89|333.71|559.76|640.59,other,1,2,1,"Figure 12. System prompt for Phase 3 (Evidence-Closed Adjudication). The prompt instantiates the agent as a final adjudicator operating under a strictly evidence-closed constraint. At this stage, all tool calls and information retrieval actions are prohibited; the agent must synthesize final primary and minor emotion predictions solely from the semantic and acoustic evidence accumulated during Phase 2. The prompt explicitly requires justification for the selected primary emotion, retained minor emotions, and the resolution of any previously predicted tie cases, ensuring causal traceability and auditability of the final decision.",88,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,8.966,1,1,0,0,0,0,1,RobotoMono-Regular|RobotoMono-Bold,6.984,6.984,6.984,color,8,#FFEEEE|#C35656|#D68C8C|#FEEBEB|#E5AFAF|#FFEDED|#F0CCCC|#FAE3E3,0.9439,,,
