icml-2026-5d3146110f97,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,3,Density sketch contrasts reverse-entropy mode seeking with cross-entropy mass covering.,single_column,311.00|100.23|588.00|407.11,conceptual_diagram,1,1,1,"(Schulman et al., 2015), Figure 2. Illustration of PPO (Schulman et al., relative entropy (mode- 2017), and GRPO (Shao seeking) and cross-entropy et al., 2024), are often em- (mass-covering) for fitting ployed, with an additional a target p∗ (G is the set of entropy regularization term Gaussian distributions). that penalizes the deviation of the model from the pretrained one. This process amounts to solving the following",66,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI9|CMSY6|CMSY9,9.963,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMR10|CMSY10|CMMI10|CMMIB10,1.559,9.963,11.955,color,8,#051976|#31408B|#D9D1DE|#7F85B2|#F4B3AE|#94A8C2|#5B68A4|#DE837C,0.0548,,,
icml-2026-5d3146110f97,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 3,6,"Three probability sketches illustrate large batch, small batch, and baseline-subtracted updates.",page_width,36.89|20.00|559.60|178.66,other,4,3,1,"Figure 3. Demonstration of the effect of weight baseline. The orange and blue curves represent the probability pθ (o|q) before and after update, and the magenta arrows represent the weights. (a) When the batch size is large, the distribution mode coverage is good. Though bad responses have positive weights, the correct ones have larger weights to push the distribution updates in the right direction. (b) When the batch size is small, some modes (e.g., the good one in the middle) may not be sampled. Without weight baseline subtraction, the dominant positive weights of the bad responses lead to wrong update directions. (c) With weight baseline subtraction, the bad responses will appropriately be penalized, leading to the desired update direction.",121,8,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR9|CMMIB9,8.966,0,0,1,1,0,0,2,CMR12|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMR7|CMBX12|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,1.701,7.622,8.966,color,8,#87AED8|#E5B39C|#BDCEE3|#F9D8C5|#F0EBE9|#F6F1ED|#EAE4E2|#F7CAB3,0.2384,,,
