icml-2026-65a15e969ebf,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,abstract,main,Figure 1,1,"Visual abstract contrasting standard gradient-update RL with test-time JitRL retrieval, advantage estimation, and logit adjustment.",page_width,57.37|45.15|559.44|352.03,qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"tion advantages on-the-fly. These estimates are Figure 1. While standard RL performs policy gradient updates during training using previous trajectories, JitRL operates at test then used to directly modulate the LLM’s out- time. Specifically, it retrieves trajectories relevant to the current put logits. We theoretically prove that this ad- state to estimate advantages A, subsequently refining the output ditive update rule is the exact closed-form solu- logits through a KL-regularized policy optimization objective. tion to the KL-constrained policy optimization objective. Extensive experiments on WebArena",85,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI9,8.966,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,6.974,9.963,14.346,color,8,#FDE3C8|#D9EFFC|#DAF0FD|#97908A|#FEE3C6|#EEDCC8|#FFE9CE|#FDE3CA,0.624,,,
icml-2026-65a15e969ebf,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,3,Cross-column overview of inference retrieval-to-logit-update loop and episode-end memory update loop.,page_width,36.89|20.00|560.04|295.65,pipeline,1,2,1,"Figure 2. Overview of the Just-In-Time Reinforcement Learning (JitRL) framework. The system operates in a continuous loop: (1) In the Inference (top), the agent retrieves relevant past experiences N(s) from the non-parametric memory M. The base LLM’s logits z are then adjusted in closed-form (z′ = z + βA(cid:98)) using the estimated advantage A derived from historical returns, enabling test-time policy improvement without gradient updates. (2) In the Memory Update (bottom), completed trajectories are analyzed by an evaluator to compute discounted returns G . These new experiences are stored back into M, allowing the agent to evolve its policy across episodes. t",103,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI9|CMEX9,8.966,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,TimesNewRomanPSMT|CambriaMath|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|TimesNewRomanPS-BoldMT|Calibri,5.276,8.457,10.842,color,7,#FCEEE3|#D9E3F4|#B3AFB1|#FCEEE2|#FEF3E8|#FCEEE4|#F1EAE7,0.888,,,
