icml-2026-6b81cf37c92f,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,2,"Flow diagram connects student rollout, multimodal and unimodal logits, visual target construction, and gradient steering.",page_width,36.89|20.00|559.44|191.24,pipeline|conceptual_diagram|qualitative_grid|image_montage,1,3,1,"Figure 2. Overview of Visual Gradient Steering (VGS). (Left) Given a multimodal query (Image I and Prompt x), we sample a rollout τ from the student policy and compute log-probabilities from both the student and teacher models under multimodal (I,x) and unimodal (x, text-only) contexts. (Middle) We decompose the standard monolithic objective into two distinct components: a Language Prior (L ) that matches the teacher’s text-only distribution, and a Visual Grounding objective (L ) that targets a constructed distribution Lang Vis q∗ isolating the teacher’s visual information gain. (Right) Our geometric analysis reveals that standard distillation (L ) acts as a T Standard passive compromise between these often orthogonal objectives. VGS explicitly steers the gradient update toward the visual subspace (L ), prioritizing perceptual fidelity over generic language modeling. Vis",129,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI9|CMSY9,8.966,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,8.966,8.966,8.966,color,8,#CDCDFF|#E0E9E8|#83546E|#9D879A|#9BACAF|#DDBAC2|#EDD7CF|#CED6F5,0.3149,,,
icml-2026-6b81cf37c92f,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 3,4,Three VDS-bin angle plots provide the gradient-geometry diagnostic; the legend shows mean plus or minus 0.5 STD.,page_width,36.89|20.00|559.44|193.81,box,1,2,1,"Figure 3. Geometric Analysis of Gradient Dynamics. (a) As visual dependency increases, the angle between Language and Visual gradients widens, approaching orthogonality in high-dependency regions. The emergence of obtuse angles (> 90◦, dashed box) at the extreme specifically motivates the Language Preservation regularizer (Eq. 16) to prevent gradient conflict. (b, c) The standard monolithic gradient (∇L ) acts as a passive bisector, maintaining a relatively static compromise orientation (≈ 40◦ − 50◦) relative to both Standard components, failing to fully align with the visual signal even when perceptual necessity is maximal (Bin 9).",89,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR9|CMSY9,8.966,0,0,0,1,0,0,1,NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,8.966,8.966,8.966,color,8,#6D9188|#577089|#D31E5F|#1F1E9B|#B296AD|#BDB1BC|#E26482|#CDC4CA,0.0799,,,
icml-2026-6b81cf37c92f,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 4,5,"Four loss-dynamics panels contrast standard, two VGS strengths, and VGS-LP over all versus high-VDS bins.",page_width,36.89|20.00|560.56|194.38,other,2,3,1,"Figure 4. Training Dynamics. We compare the evolution of decomposed loss components during training across different methods. (a) Visual Grounding (L ): VGS (blue) significantly accelerates visual learning compared to the standard monolithic baseline (L , Vis Standard green), especially for high-dependency tokens (Bins 7–9). (b) Language Prior (L ): Without regularization, aggressive visual steering Lang (γ = 2.0, dark blue) causes the language prior to diverge (“unlearning”), particularly in high-conflict visual regimes (Bins 7–9). Our final method with Language Preservation (L , pink) successfully prevents this degradation while maintaining superior visual grounding. VGS-LP",92,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMSY9|CMR9,8.966,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,8.966,8.966,8.966,color,8,#F476AF|#64898C|#8C78DE|#1C179C|#506990|#ADA8C0|#BEBBCC|#D7D1E1,0.1906,,,
icml-2026-6b81cf37c92f,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,table,results,main,Table 1,6,Main seven-benchmark comparison of standard OPD and VGS for 2B and 4B students using Acc@1 and Acc@16.,page_width,55.44|161.39|539.20|364.43,table,1,1,1,"Table 1. Main Results on Vision-Language Reasoning Benchmarks. We compare the distillation performance of Visual Gradient Steering (VGS) against the standard monolithic baseline. All student models (2B and 4B) are distilled from the same Qwen3-VL- 8B-Instruct teacher trained with GRPO. VGS consistently outperforms the standard approach across all benchmarks, achieving higher accuracy in both greedy decoding (Acc@1) and stochastic sampling (Acc@16).",63,5,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,8.966,1,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMSY7,9.044,9.044,9.044,color,8,#0C850C|#58A956|#79BC79|#A5D0A4|#379B37|#C6E2C5|#D7EBD7|#248F22,0.0958,6,6,1
