icml-2026-6b81cf37c92f,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 7,13,Dual-axis trajectory shows standard and visual gradient norms and cosine similarity used to justify fixed eta.,page_width,36.89|240.67|559.44|547.55,line,1,1,1,"Figure 7. Evolution of Gradient Norm Components. We track the magnitudes of the standard gradient (purple) and visual gradient (green), along with their cosine similarity (blue) for the Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct student during standard on-policy distillation. All three components exhibit stability across training steps, justifying our approximation of the adaptive scaling factor η (γ) as a fixed VGS constant to reduce computational overhead.",61,4,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI9|CMR9,8.966,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|CMSY10|CMMI10|CMR10|CMR7,6.974,9.963,9.963,color,8,#5852EC|#B833D9|#6F70E7|#64B9A5|#B1ACDA|#B376D7|#E4DFEE|#72C5B1,0.0778,,,
