icml-2026-7207f7ebdc88,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 3,4,two-stage softened ternarization relay,page_width,36.89|20.00|561.01|161.58,line|conceptual_diagram|qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 3. Illustration of the softened ternarization (ST) process. For a linear layer, taking its pre-trained weights W as the initialization point (t = 0), ST employs a learnable two-stage relay of differentiable ternarization and hard ternarization to ensure stable convergence. In the first stage, ST produces an asymptotic ternary output by performing continuous quantization based on the transformed weights Wˆ . It relies on a novel smooth transition function f(·) to gradually evolve from the identity mapping to differentiable ternarization via a sequence of continuous mappings with progressively increasing sharpness along the normalized calibration time state 0 < t ≤ γ. In the second stage γ < t ≤ 1, ST proceeds with hard ternarization to get a final solution. Notations are clarified in the Method section.",122,7,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMMI9|CMR9|CMSY9,8.966,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,CambriaMath|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|TimesNewRomanPSMT,6.317,8.625,8.966,color,8,#E63431|#F2A59C|#F3867D|#F9CDC8|#7D423E|#FBBAB2|#FCDAD6|#AD7771,0.2978,,,
