icml-2026-b4d312dbe2a3,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 1,2,"PAR training/inference architecture with Tθ, vθ, multi-scale down/up-sampling",page_width,52.18|20.00|560.92|253.45,pipeline|architecture,1,1,1,"Figure 1 Overview of PAR. PAR comprises the autoregressive (AR) transformer T θ and the flow-based backbone decoder v . During training, we downsample a backbone x ∈ RL×3 into multi-scale representations {x1,...,x}. θ AR transformer performs next-scale prediction, producing conditional embeddings (z1,...,zn) from (bos,...,xn−1). The shared flow-based decoder learns to denoise backbones xi at each scale conditioned on zi. At inference, PAR autoregressively generates xi until the final structure x is constructed.",76,6,SFRM0900|SFTI0900|ByteSans-Bold|CMMI9|CMBX9,8.966,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,,,,,color,8,#BFDBF7|#FDD0F3|#69727A|#8697A1|#EAEFDA|#514752|#C5B8BC|#BEDBF6,0.5534,,,
