icml-2026-ba706ff6b691,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,introduction,main,Figure 1,2,"Visualize full-precision, quantized, and corrected denoising trajectories and the role of cumulative error.",page_width,52.87|20.00|559.14|263.58,qualitative_grid,1,2,1,"Figure 1 Visualization of Error Propagation and Correction in Quantized Diffusion Models. The gray path represents the iterative denoising process of the full-precision model µ, while the brown-red path represents that of the quantized model µ˜. Affected by cumulative errors δ , its output gradually deviates from µ. The green path represents the t denoising process after online correction of cumulative errors, with outputs better aligned with the full-precision model.",69,4,SFRM0900|ByteSans-Bold|CMMI9|CMR9|CMMI6,8.966,0,1,0,0,1,0,2,,,,,color,8,#DBBBB9|#CCDAC6|#A5887F|#D6C4CB|#6C4B44|#BAC7AC|#BAB2A7|#C6D5B9,0.3235,,,
