icml-2026-ca6b03466916,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 13,48,Tests the effect of MaxRL rollout count on GSM8K coverage.,page_width,52.87|20.00|542.73|197.84,qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 13: (Effect of number of training rollouts in the GSM8K setting) For MaxRL, increase in number of rollouts N directly leads to an increase in the approximation order T of the maximum likelihood objective that the finite sample MaxRL optimizes. Here we compare the final checkpoint resulting from training with different values of T(= Number of rollouts) but otherwise identical training setup on the GSM8K setting. Increasing compute smoothly translates into performance gain, with the highest amount of gain for higher pass@k.",84,3,SFRM0800|SFBX0800|SFCC0800|CMMI8|CMR8,7.97,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,DejaVuSans,4.425,7.235,10.066,color,8,#DE5C4F|#8384A3|#FCC2B5|#F3DEDA|#F1CDC8|#F89B8C|#CBB7BF|#80494F,0.1042,,,
