icml-2026-d6b2488d4518,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 10,19,跨 layer 展示 Q-FIT calibration behavior，并比较 E1M2 KV 与 Q-FIT 对 quantized training loss 的影响。,page_width,36.89|20.00|560.56|228.37,other,2,2,1,"Figure 10. (a) Layer-wise calibration behavior with Q-FIT. We visualize key-cache statistics before and after RoPE across multiple layers, together with the corresponding calibration error heatmaps. (b) Training loss comparison under different QAT settings. Using an E1M2 KV cache consistently results in lower training loss compared to TAQ, which adopts E2M1 by default. Incorporating Q-FIT further reduces the training loss relative to TAQ-only variants, indicating more stable and effective quantized training (Model: R1-Qwen-14B).",73,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,8.966,0,1,0,1,1,0,3,TimesNewRomanPSMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CambriaMath,5.927,7.368,8.966,color,8,#B5B994|#335F8B|#6B7B3E|#4B1061|#3C3D82|#45327D|#3B7E78|#7F836D,0.2441,,,
icml-2026-d6b2488d4518,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 11,19,展示 MXFP4 block rotation 前后的 activation outlier redistribution，以及 Q-FIT 与 down-projection unquantized 的 loss 对照。,page_width,36.89|156.02|559.44|462.90,other,2,2,1,"Figure 11. Effect of block rotation and Q-FIT in MXFP4 W4A4. (a) Activation magnitude before and after block rotation, showing a small number of extreme outlier channels. After block-wise Hadamard rotation, outliers are redistributed across channels. (b) Training loss comparison under different QAT settings. Applying block rotation with Q-FIT achieves a training loss comparable to leaving the MLP down-projection layer unquantized, and consistently improves over TAQ with fully quantized down-projection (Model: R1-Qwen-14B).",72,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,8.966,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|TimesNewRomanPSMT|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,2.042,8.966,9.247,color,8,#6D815A|#403F81|#ED4736|#F24D37|#A4B29A|#820026|#F5593D|#4D6772,0.2061,,,
