icml-2026-da310238c4b0,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,4,"Connect KL projection, implicit teacher, dense supervision, and curriculum iteration.",page_width,36.89|20.00|559.75|214.14,pipeline|image_montage,1,3,1,"Figure 2. Overview of Physical safety Alignment for Constrained Trajectories. PACT frames physical safety alignment as projecting a pretrained diffusion policy µ onto the CMDP feasible set Π via a KL-regularized constrained objective. For fixed multipliers, the ϕ safe score function of the optimal aligned policy is defined as an implicit safety teacher by combining the base score with differentiable cost gradients (Theorem 3.1). We distill this teacher into a student diffusion policy π using self-rollouts with direct and dense supervision θ across diffusion time and in a self-evolving manner without manual demonstrations or rewards. A curriculum schedule progressively increases constraint strength, yielding controlled policy shifts and monotonic safety improvement over iterations (Theorem 3.3).",116,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR6|CMMI9,8.966,1,1,0,1,0,0,2,TimesNewRomanPSMT|TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMMI7|CMMI10|CMR10,3.698,6.913,9.058,color,8,#D6E5CF|#EFD9D9|#A66663|#A5B6B0|#A89083|#E7C0C0|#C5D5BE|#F0D6CE,0.1802,,,
