icml-2026-e0395b78826d,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 1,7,Two panels plot overcharged tokens and plausible sequences against m for Algorithm 1.,page_width,53.74|20.00|560.22|265.62,qualitative_grid,2,4,1,"Figure 1: Misreporting the tokenization of outputs generated by different LLMs using Algorithm 1. Panel (a) shows the percentage of tokens overcharged by an unfaithful provider who misreports the tokenization of the outputs to 600 prompts from the LMSYS Chatbot Arena platform using Algorithm 1, for different values of m. Panel (b) shows the fraction of outputs to the same 600 prompts where Algorithm 1 returns a tokenization that is plausible under top-p sampling, for different values of m. In both panels, we set the temperature to 1.3 and use top-p sampling with p = 0.95. In panel (b), we repeat the experiment 5 times to obtain 90% confidence intervals.",111,5,SFRM1000|SFBX1000|CMR10|CMMI10,9.963,0,1,1,1,1,0,4,CMR10|SFRM0900|CMMI10|CMMI9,2.073,7.484,8.966,color,8,#C8DAE1|#8FB7BE|#F09A77|#FAB79D|#F8E8E1|#C1BAC4|#EED8D1|#989DB1,0.2524,,,
icml-2026-e0395b78826d,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 2,9,Three model panels show additional revenue as overcharged tokens across m and top-p settings.,page_width,53.64|20.00|560.22|202.39,qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 2: Additional revenue from misreporting the tokenization of outputs using Algorithm 2. The panels show the percentage of tokens overcharged by an unfaithful provider who misreports the tokenization of the outputs generated by an LLM to 600 prompts from the LMSYS Chatbot Arena platform using the reporting policies πH implemented by Algorithm 2, for different values of m and p. The dashed vertical lines m correspond to the optimal value of m. Here, we set the temperature of the model to 1.3 and repeat each experiment 5 times to obtain 90% confidence intervals. Refer to Appendix C.1 for additional results using alternative temperature values and other LLMs.",110,5,SFRM1000|SFBX1000|CMR10|CMMI10|SFTT0800,9.963,0,1,0,1,1,1,3,CMR10|SFTT0900|CMR12|CMMI10|CMMI12,1.936,4.989,8.966,color,8,#DCEFDA|#FDE4E9|#95C0B4|#E7F4EC|#A6D6C8|#F6DCE0|#D2EAE1|#FBE4E8,0.6337,,,
icml-2026-e0395b78826d,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 3,10,Three model panels show utility gain versus provider profit margin and top-p.,page_width,53.62|20.00|559.38|202.39,qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 3: Financial gain from misreporting the tokenization of outputs using Algorithm 2. The panels show the utility gain that an unfaithful provider who misreports the tokenization of the outputs generated by an LLM to 600 prompts from the LMSYS Chatbot Arena platform using Algorithm 2 can achieve, for different values of p and the provider’s profit margin ρ . The dashed vertical lines represent the o minimum margin above which misreporting is financially viable according to Eq. 4. Here, for each value of p, we run Algorithm 2 using the optimal number of iterations m shown in Figure 2, set the temperature of the model to 1.3 and repeat each experiment 5 times to obtain 90% confidence intervals. Refer to Figure 7 of Appendix C.1 for additional results using alternative temperature values and other LLMs.",138,6,SFRM1000|SFBX1000|CMR10|CMMI10|CMMI7,9.963,0,1,0,1,1,1,3,CMR10|SFTT0900|CMMI10|CMMI7,1.382,4.989,8.966,color,8,#85C7AA|#FDE0E5|#50A8A1|#DBEEEA|#E9F4F7|#C1E2D7|#FDE4E9|#D6A0B0,0.4206,,,
