icml-2026-e0395b78826d,ICML,oral,foundation_200,figure,appendix,appendix,Figure 5,23,"3x3 grid shows fraction of outputs with a longer plausible tokenization across models, p, and temperature.",page_width,53.49|20.00|559.93|126.09,qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 5 shows the fraction of generated outputs for which Algorithm 2 finds a longer plausible tokenization. We observe that the higher the values of p and temperature, the higher the likelihood that Algorithm 2 finds plausible longer tokenizations. Figure 6 shows the percentage of tokens overcharged by an unfaithful provider who uses Algorithm 2. We observe that the percentage of overcharged tokens is unimodal with respect to the number of iterations m, and the higher the value of p and the temperature, the higher the percentage of overcharged tokens, as the top-p sets become larger and the likelihood that a longer tokenization is plausible increases. Figure 7 shows the relative increase in utility that a provider using Algorithm 2 can achieve under pay-per-token compared to the faithful reporting policy π , as a function of their margin ρ for output tokens. 0",142,5,SFRM1000|CMMI10,9.963,0,1,1,1,0,0,3,SFBX1200|SFBX1440,11.955,11.955,14.346,grayscale,0,,0.0,,,
