icml-2026-fea2d498a956,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,method,main,Figure 2,3,Pairs the decoder slot/token/termination heads with PL sampling and RLOO optimization.,page_width,36.89|20.00|559.44|233.79,architecture,2,3,1,"Figure 2. (a) Generative Decoder Architecture. At generation step i, the Transformer processes the partial sequence y (augmented i−1 with boundary tokens) to produce contextual embeddings h. The embedding h predicts the termination probability (Step 2.1). The EOS remaining embeddings h represent candidate insertion slots (dotted boxes), parameterizing the location distribution p(z |y ) (Step k i i−1 2.2). Conditioned on a selected slot (e.g., z = 4), the content head predicts the next token x (Step 3). (b) Policy-gradient optimization i i with Monte Carlo–estimated insertion orders q (σ | y ). The expectation over q (σ | y ) in Eq. 12 is approximated using θ <i L θ <i L",114,8,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|CMMI9|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal|CMR9,8.966,0,1,0,1,0,0,2,BanglaSangamMN-Bold|BanglaSangamMN|ArialMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi|TimesNewRomanPSMT,5.93,5.93,8.966,color,8,#73605A|#96807B|#9A8781|#BDADA4|#654943|#87746F|#A38C85|#D5C9BC,0.0552,,,
