icml-2026-fea2d498a956,ICML,spotlight,foundation_200,figure,results,main,Figure 5,8,Shows a four-stage SMILES insertion trajectory ending in termination.,page_width,36.89|20.00|559.59|151.84,line|qualitative_grid,1,3,1,"Figure 5. An example of generating a SMILES sample via the Insertion Process. The learned generation process is phased into four stages: 1) At Stage 1 (Step 0), the model starts with an empty string. 2) From Step 1 to 17 in Stage 2, the model first lays out the molecule’s skeleton by generating only matching parentheses and digit pairs (ring-closure markers). 3) In Stage 3, the model then inserts atom symbols into this scaffold to form the full SMILES string. 4) Finally, at Step 44, the model signals termination, and the generated molecule stays the same as that in Step 43.",103,6,NimbusRomNo9L-Regu|NimbusRomNo9L-ReguItal,8.966,0,1,0,0,0,0,1,CourierNewPS-BoldMT|Arial-BoldMT|NimbusRomNo9L-Medi,5.4,6.172,8.966,color,8,#79ADCE|#E2866E|#DEE9EE|#EF5558|#FEEEE3|#FED2C5|#FAAC87|#9ED6B6,0.2617,,,
